{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780660319,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1437e6e001mC8PTREOEAQLQF","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e143727a0017PRNRqe5CTYADm","type":"tool","id":"call_c98f5cd9c4044f728e51a1b7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\nindex 095fb70932a..b3b90611adf 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ The doctor companion line now prints its policy word. It reads `Also: /doctor:up\n \n #### Six Paths and Two Rates\n \n-The transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the runs that loaded a workflow over every owned run. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n+The transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the `command` and `skill` runs over every owned run. An `otherMode` run sits in its denominator only. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n \n #### Every Shape a Load Takes\n \n@@ -248,4 +248,4 @@ The no-edit and cue rows ran the old and new patterns side by side. The hook row\n - **If you want hook health in `/doctor:setup`:** send one prompt. Set `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` only to log the skill label and error text.\n - **If you read the `offered` count of the transcript summary:** a command on the partner side no longer counts as an offer. Run logs now keep `offeredAs`.\n - **If you match on an advisor command id:** replace `command-create-skill` with `command-create-sk-skill`.\n-- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no alias.\n+- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no command file. A typed `/create:skill` still reads as `/create:sk-skill`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\nindex 15b5129c63d..a8117b5ebfe 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"command row embedding\"\n   - \"vec_cmd table\"\n   - \"command meaning anchor\"\n-version: 1.0.3.0\n+version: 1.0.4.0\n ---\n \n # Command Meaning Matching\n@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ A command row used to pass only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. A\n \n ### Command Vectors\n \n-`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 46 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n+`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 47 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n \n `skill_graph_scan` embeds that text into a separate `vec_cmd_<dim>` table. The table carries no foreign key, and the skill vector table is left untouched. A row whose text hash has not changed is skipped. A stored row that the deriver no longer generates is pruned.\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\nindex 91938fd0e93..9a79b97caf0 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n ---\n title: \"Skill Advisor: Manual Testing Playbook\"\n description: \"Canonical sk-doc manual testing playbook for the Skill Advisor manual scenario corpus across the native command surface, runtime hooks, compatibility, daemon state, indexing, lifecycle, scorer and Python compatibility workflows.\"\n-version: 0.8.12.0\n+version: 0.8.13.0\n ---\n \n # Skill Advisor: Manual Testing Playbook\n@@ -35,8 +35,6 @@ A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its\n \n This playbook provides 53 scenario files across 9 categories, one of them a live conversation scenario, validating the Skill Advisor surface. Scenario IDs use a multi-prefix scheme: `NC` for the native command surface, `CL` for CLI hooks plus plugin behavior, `CP` for compatibility plus disable controls, `OP` for operator H5 states, `AU` for auto-update daemon behavior, `AI` for auto-indexing, `LC` for lifecycle routing, `SC` for scorer fusion and `PC` for Python compatibility.\n \n-> **Numbering note (gap-09).** The directory layout skips slot `09--*` between `scorer-fusion` and `python-compat`. This mirrors the `feature-catalog/` 05-gap pattern and is an intentional historical reservation from initial scaffold design. The gap is preserved to keep spec-folder cross-reference stability across packets. Do not renumber.\n-\n Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 53 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n \n ### Realistic Test Model\n@@ -81,7 +79,7 @@ npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n - Exit code for shell commands.\n - Hook stdout and stderr captured separately when hook scripts are involved.\n - Final user-facing verdict with rationale.\n-- Triage notes for every `FAIL`, `PARTIAL` or `SKIP`.\n+- Triage notes for every `FAIL` or `SKIP`.\n \n ---\n \n@@ -100,7 +98,7 @@ npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n ### Inputs Required\n \n 1. `manual-testing-playbook.md`.\n-2. Referenced per-feature files under `manual-testing-playbook/NN__category_name/`.\n+2. Referenced per-feature files under each category folder, such as `manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/`.\n 3. Scenario execution evidence.\n 4. Feature-to-scenario coverage map.\n 5. Triage notes for all non-pass outcomes.\n@@ -118,14 +116,13 @@ For each executed scenario, check:\n \n Scenario verdict:\n - `PASS`: all acceptance checks true.\n-- `PARTIAL`: core behavior works but non-critical evidence or metadata is incomplete.\n - `FAIL`: expected behavior missing, contradictory output appears, prompt text leaks or a critical check failed.\n - `SKIP`: a real sandbox, dependency or runtime blocker prevents execution and is documented.\n \n ### Feature Verdict Rules\n \n - `PASS`: all mapped scenarios for the feature are `PASS`.\n-- `PARTIAL`: at least one mapped scenario is `PARTIAL`, none are `FAIL`.\n+- `SKIP`: no mapped scenario is `FAIL` and at least one is `SKIP`.\n - `FAIL`: any mapped scenario is `FAIL`.\n \n ### Release Readiness Rule\n@@ -152,7 +149,7 @@ This section records wave planning for the canonical Skill Advisor manual test p\n ### Recommended Wave Plan\n \n - **Wave 1**: `NC-001..NC-012` native command-surface behavior.\n-- **Wave 2**: `CL-001`, `CL-004..CL-010` runtime hooks, the OpenCode plugin, CLI fallback and the goal plugin.\n+- **Wave 2**: `CL-001`, `CL-005..CL-010` runtime hooks, the OpenCode plugin, CLI fallback and the goal plugin.\n - **Wave 3**: `CP-001..CP-004` compatibility and disable controls.\n - **Wave 4**: `OP-001..OP-003` H5 operator states.\n - **Wave 5**: `AU-001..AU-005` auto-update daemon behavior.\n@@ -186,7 +183,7 @@ This category validates native command-surface scenarios `NC-001..NC-012`.\n \n ## 8. CLI HOOKS AND PLUGIN\n \n-This category validates cli hooks and plugin scenarios `CL-001`, `CL-004..CL-010`.\n+This category validates cli hooks and plugin scenarios `CL-001`, `CL-005..CL-010`.\n \n | ID | Scenario | File |\n |---|---|---|\n@@ -347,7 +344,7 @@ The catalog uses 7 groups. The playbook uses 9 categories. Mapping is intentiona\n | `scorer-fusion` | `scorer-fusion` | 1:1 mapping |\n | `cli-surface` | `native-cli-tools` plus `cli-hooks-and-plugin` | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: native command-surface scenarios in 01, CLI hook plus plugin invocation scenarios in 02 |\n | `hooks-and-plugin` | `cli-hooks-and-plugin` (primary) plus `compat-and-disable` (rollback states) | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: happy-path hook behavior in 02, disable plus rollback flags in 03 |\n-| `python-compat` | `python-compat` | 1:1 mapping (note gap-09 is intentional per playbook §1) |\n+| `python-compat` | `python-compat` | 1:1 mapping |\n | (none) | `compat-and-disable` | Compat plus disable flags cut across multiple catalog groups. No single catalog group owns them |\n | (none) | `operator-h5` | H5 operator state scenarios cut across catalog groups. No single catalog group owns them |\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\nindex 095fb70932a..b3b90611adf 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ The doctor companion line now prints its policy word. It reads `Also: /doctor:up\n \n #### Six Paths and Two Rates\n \n-The transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the runs that loaded a workflow over every owned run. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n+The transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the `command` and `skill` runs over every owned run. An `otherMode` run sits in its denominator only. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n \n #### Every Shape a Load Takes\n \n@@ -248,4 +248,4 @@ The no-edit and cue rows ran the old and new patterns side by side. The hook row\n - **If you want hook health in `/doctor:setup`:** send one prompt. Set `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` only to log the skill label and error text.\n - **If you read the `offered` count of the transcript summary:** a command on the partner side no longer counts as an offer. Run logs now keep `offeredAs`.\n - **If you match on an advisor command id:** replace `command-create-skill` with `command-create-sk-skill`.\n-- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no alias.\n+- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no command file. A typed `/create:skill` still reads as `/create:sk-skill`.\ndiff --git a/.ski