-> 2. Save JSON to `/tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/sad-002.json` -> 3. Compare `data.recommendations[0].confidence`, `data.recommendations[1].confidence` and `data.ambiguous` | Envelope status is `ok`. Top recommendations are plausible for the prompt. Close top-two results set `ambiguous: true`. Lane attribution remains prompt-safe | Unit test command output: `RUN  v4.1.6 .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`; `✓ tests/handlers/advisor-recommend.vitest.ts (22 tests) 20ms`; `✓ tests/legacy/advisor-renderer.vitest.ts (13 tests) 4ms`; `Test Files  2 passed (2)`; `Tests  35 passed (35)`; `Start at  03:42:49`; `Duration  444ms (transform 207ms, setup 19ms, import 279ms, tests 24ms, environment 0ms)`. Broad prompt advisor output values: `status: \"ok\"`, `recommendations: []`, `ambiguous: false`, `freshness: \"unavailable\"`, `trustState.reason: \"advisor_unavailable\"`, `generation: 9476`, `checkedAt: \"2026-07-03T01:43:04.878Z\"`, `warnings: [\"advisor_unavailable\"]`, `abstainReasons: [\"Skill advisor freshness is unavailable; returning fail-open empty recommendations.\"]`. Legacy prompt advisor output values: `status: \"ok\"`, `recommendations: []`, `ambiguous: false`, `freshness: \"unavailable\"`, `trustState.reason: \"advisor_unavailable\"`, `generation: 9476`, `checkedAt: \"2026-07-03T01:43:05.041Z\"`, `warnings: [\"advisor_unavailable\"]`, `abstainReasons: [\"Skill advisor freshness is unavailable; returning fail-open empty recommendations.\"]`. `/tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/sad-002.json` was not created because this run's allowed write paths were restricted to this scenario file only. | BLOCKED - native advisor freshness was `unavailable` with `reason: \"advisor_unavailable\"`, so no top-two recommendations existed to compare and `ambiguous: true` could not be evaluated. | 1. Inspect scorer ambiguity threshold; 2. Re-run handler and renderer tests; 3. Check lane attribution for prompt leakage; 4. Review feature catalog ambiguity entry |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== CL scenarios ===\nbrief-command-policy-word.md\nclaude-user-prompt-submit.md\ngoal-opencode-plugin-conversation.md\ngoal-opencode-plugin.md\nopencode-plugin-bridge.md\nskill-advisor-cli-fallback.md\nvibe-command-documents.md\n=== count all scenario files ===\n      53\n=== PARTIAL anywhere in playbook pkg ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/ambiguous-brief-rendering.md:62:| SAD-002 | Ambiguous recommendation rendering | Confirm close recommendations are surfaced as ambiguity instead of false certainty | `Role: Skill Advisor MCP operator. Context: cross-domain prompt spanning documentation review, prompt improvement and OpenCode system work. Action: call advisor_recommend with topK 2 and attribution enabled, then inspect top-two confidence values and the ambiguity flag. Format: return PASS, PARTIAL or FAIL with top-two skill IDs, confidence values and ambiguity state.` | 1. `advisor_recommend({\"prompt\":\"Review the OpenCode docs and improve the prompt package for a release note workflow.\",\"options\":{\"topK\":2,\"includeAttribution\":true,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true}})` -> 2. Save JSON to `/tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/sad-002.json` -> 3. Compare `data.recommendations[0].confidence`, `data.recommendations[1].confidence` and `data.ambiguous` | Envelope status is `ok`. Top recommendations are plausible for the prompt. Close top-two results set `ambiguous: true`. Lane attribution remains prompt-safe | Unit test command output: `RUN  v4.1.6 .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`; `✓ tests/handlers/advisor-recommend.vitest.ts (22 tests) 20ms`; `✓ tests/legacy/advisor-renderer.vitest.ts (13 tests) 4ms`; `Test Files  2 passed (2)`; `Tests  35 passed (35)`; `Start at  03:42:49`; `Duration  444ms (transform 207ms, setup 19ms, import 279ms, tests 24ms, environment 0ms)`. Broad prompt advisor output values: `status: \"ok\"`, `recommendations: []`, `ambiguous: false`, `freshness: \"unavailable\"`, `trustState.reason: \"advisor_unavailable\"`, `generation: 9476`, `checkedAt: \"2026-07-03T01:43:04.878Z\"`, `warnings: [\"advisor_unavailable\"]`, `abstainReasons: [\"Skill advisor freshness is unavailable; returning fail-open empty recommendations.\"]`. Legacy prompt advisor output values: `status: \"ok\"`, `recommendations: []`, `ambiguous: false`, `freshness: \"unavailable\"`, `trustState.reason: \"advisor_unavailable\"`, `generation: 9476`, `checkedAt: \"2026-07-03T01:43:05.041Z\"`, `warnings: [\"advisor_unavailable\"]`, `abstainReasons: [\"Skill advisor freshness is unavailable; returning fail-open empty recommendations.\"]`. `/tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/sad-002.json` was not created because this run's allowed write paths were restricted to this scenario file only. | BLOCKED - native advisor freshness was `unavailable` with `reason: \"advisor_unavailable\"`, so no top-two recommendations existed to compare and `ambiguous: true` could not be evaluated. | 1. Inspect scorer ambiguity threshold; 2. Re-run handler and renderer tests; 3. Check lane attribution for prompt leakage; 4. Review feature catalog ambiguity entry |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \\\"=== CL scenarios ===\\\" && ls -1 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/ && echo \\\"=== count all scenario files ===\\\" && find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook -name '*.md' -mindepth 2 | wc -l && echo \\\"=== PARTIAL anywhere in playbook pkg ===\\\" && grep -rn \\\"PARTIAL\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/ | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780696525,"end":1794780698504}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780708864,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e144149d001YAzX5pUtEK5o7l","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e143f50a0018bxaD0AxOU0F0S","type":"tool","id":"call_42bfc8feefab4ea986a02798","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"leaf-scopes.json\" --include=*.cjs --include=*.mjs --include=*.ts --include=*.js --include=*.md .skilled | grep -v \"leaf-scopes.json:\" | head -30"},"output":".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.10.md:65:The block's \"Before you start\" step opens with `bash .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh provision .` for a fresh clone and `git config --local skilled.trustRepoHooks true` for a clone that should run the hooks. The removal steps name the two feature-catalog files and regenerate `graph-metadata.json` with `regenerate-skill-derived.cjs`. The add steps name `leaf-scopes.json` and the surface-count lines the documentation claim checker reads.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/README.md:150:3. Add the packet's paths to the `ROUTER.md` maps and section 8, and its `surfaceDetection` block to its `mode-registry.json` entry (`stack-detection.md` section 2 reads it). Update any surface-count wording that `verify-doc-claims.cjs` checks in the hub's `README.md` and `SKILL.md`. `phase-detection.md` names the surfaces without a count. A packet copied from an existing surface has the same leaf set as that surface, so `generate-leaf-manifest.cjs --write` stops with `MODE_LEAF_SET_COLLISION`. Give each of the two modes its own `leafScopes` in a new `leaf-scopes.json` at the hub root, in the array format `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/leaf-scopes.json` uses, or change the copy until its files differ.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.17.23.0.md:32:- **`hooks/` is Markdown-only through `leaf-scopes.json`.** The scope names its five hook docs, so the nine runtime `.ts`, `.py` and `.json` files beside them are never leaves.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.17.21.0.md:24:- **The `hooks/` leaf root is Markdown only.** Nine non-`.md` files under `hooks/` left the leaf manifest and the alias file, and `leaf-scopes.json` now limits that leaf root to Markdown. No route changed.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:102:- Every routable leaf under the five declared leaf roots, `references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, `manual-testing-playbook/` and `hooks/`, is enumerated in `leaf-manifest.json`, generated from `leaf-manifest.config.json` and narrowed by `leaf-scopes.json`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103:- `hooks/` is Markdown-only through `leaf-scopes.json`: the scope names its five hook docs, and the nine runtime `.ts`, `.py` and `.json` files beside them are never leaves. `assets/` is declared and has no docs to contribute.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.3.0.md:3:description: \"A standalone skill now reads leaf-scopes.json, so it can narrow a configured leaf root to the files its router actually selects. system-skill-advisor is the first to use it, keeping only Markdown under hooks/.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.3.0.md:17:`leaf-scopes.json` already narrowed a hub's mode to its own packet-relative subtrees. The standalone path now reads the same file through the same helpers, so one option serves both kinds of skill and a scope is spelled the same way in either.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.3.0.md:35:No action is needed. A skill with no `leaf-scopes.json`, or with an empty scope list, walks its full leaf roots exactly as before.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:3:description: \"The packet, the root-metadata contract and the standalone playbook now name leaf-scopes.json, the optional authored file that narrows a standalone skill's leaf roots, with the two codes that stop a bad scope.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:16:A standalone skill could author `leaf-scopes.json`, but nothing in this packet said so. The generator had read the file since the standalone scoping release, and `system-skill-advisor` already depends on it to keep `hooks/` Markdown-only, yet an author following the skill met the capability only in a changelog entry.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:26:- **The file is named where an author looks.** The standalone shape lists `leaf-scopes.json` as optional, and the prose says which roots it narrows and why.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:37:No action is needed. A root without `leaf-scopes.json` generates the same manifest it did before.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:71:| `leaf-scopes.json` | optional, authored | optional, authored | authored |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:90:### Why `leaf-scopes.json` is optional for both classes\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:113:Everything else carries authored semantic identity, routing policy, or a declaration only a human can make: `graph-metadata.json`, `description.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json`, `leaf-manifest.config.json`, `command-metadata.json` and `leaf-scopes.json`, plus `leaf-aliases.json` on a hub, where the projection carries real compatibility mappings rather than a derivative. `--fix` reads every one of them and never rewrites one.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:182:**A new standalone skill (S):** author `SKILL.md`, `graph-metadata.json`, and `leaf-manifest.config.json`, because that config is the single declaration that names the workflow mode and the leaf roots. Add `leaf-scopes.json` only when a configured leaf root must be narrowed to a subtree or a named set of docs. Add `command-metadata.json` only when the skill ships slash commands, and set every entry's `ownerMode` to the skill's own id. Run `--fix` to generate the manifest and the alias projection.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:184:A standalone root therefore needs exactly one required authored metadata file beyond identity. `leaf-scopes.json` and `command-metadata.json` stay optional, added only when the root needs them. That is the whole delta between a non-conforming root and a conforming one.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:188:Every authored file except `leaf-scopes.json` has a scaffold under `sk-create-skill/assets/`. The two generated files deliberately have none, because hand-editing them is what the freshness gate exists to catch. For the scope file, copy the shape from a shipped root. A standalone root reuses the hub scaffold for `command-metadata.json` and sets every entry's `ownerMode` to its own skill id.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:200:| `leaf-scopes.json` | H + S | none — copy a shipped root, such as `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-scopes.json` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:166:Verify that a standalone root authors `graph-metadata.json` and `leaf-manifest.config.json`, adds `leaf-scopes.json` only when a leaf root needs narrowing, omits hub-only declarations and generates fresh manifest files.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:172:The mode should classify the root as class S because it declares neither `mode-registry.json` nor `hub-router.json`. It should author the identity and leaf config, run the metadata gate with `--fix` and confirm that `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` are generated. It should not add `description.json` or a parent registry. When a declared leaf root needs narrowing, it should add `leaf-scopes.json` for the config's single `workflowMode` and confirm that a scope outside the declared roots fails with `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` and a scope on an undeclared mode fails with `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:30:- Expected execution process: inspect the root, confirm it declares neither `mode-registry.json` nor `hub-router.json`, author `graph-metadata.json` and `leaf-manifest.config.json`, add `leaf-scopes.json` only when a declared leaf root needs narrowing, run `ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs --fix`, confirm fresh generated files and prove both bad-scope failures.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:31:- Expected signals: class S is named, `graph-metadata.json` and `leaf-manifest.config.json` are authored, `leaf-scopes.json` is named as the optional authored file that narrows a declared leaf root for the config's single `workflowMode`, `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` are generated and hub-only files are absent. A scope outside the declared leaf roots reports `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` and a scope on an undeclared workflow mode reports `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:45:| SKL-002 | Classify standalone root metadata | Classify a standalone root and produce the correct authored and generated metadata files | `My new skill is standalone. Which root metadata files should I author and which ones should the gate generate?` | 1. `agent: Read the standalone class row in references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` -> 2. `agent: Confirm the root declares neither mode-registry.json nor hub-router.json` -> 3. `agent: Author graph-metadata.json and leaf-manifest.config.json, the required class-S set` -> 4. `agent: When a declared leaf root needs narrowing, add leaf-scopes.json naming the config's workflowMode` -> 5. `bash: node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs --fix` -> 6. `bash: node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs` -> 7. `bash: node --test .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/generate-leaf-manifest-standalone-scopes.test.cjs` | Step 1: class S is named. Step 2: both hub declarations are absent. Step 3: the required authored set is correct and no scope file is invented for a root that needs none. Step 4: the scope stays under a declared leaf root and names the configured `workflowMode`. Step 5: generated manifests are refreshed, and a scoped root's manifest lists only the scoped leaves. Step 6: the final gate is clean. Step 7: the scoped-generator suite passes, which proves `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` stops a scope outside the declared roots and `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE` stops a scope on an undeclared mode | The exact prompt, class row, root metadata listing, both gate transcripts with exit statuses, the scope failure output and the final file ownership map | PASS if the authored and generated sets match class S, any scope stays under a declared leaf root, and the final gate reports clean. FAIL if a hub-only file is present, a scope escapes the declared roots or names an undeclared mode, or generated output is hand-authored | 1. Compare the root files with the class S matrix. 2. Check that `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` match generated output. 3. Re-run the gate without `--fix` and read its exit status. 4. Compare a failing scope's `workflowMode` with `leaf-manifest.config.json` and its path with the declared `leafRoots`, which is what separates `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE` from `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:52:4. `agent: When a declared leaf root needs narrowing, add leaf-scopes.json naming the config's workflowMode`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:73:2. Compare the root file set with the class S matrix, including whether `leaf-scopes.json` was needed at all.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:95:| [`scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs`](../../scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs) | Reads `leaf-scopes.json` and fails closed on a bad scope |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/generate-leaf-manifest-standalone-scopes.test.cjs:35:    writeFile(skillDir, 'leaf-scopes.json', `${JSON.stringify({ scopes: [{\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/generate-leaf-manifest-standalone-scopes.test.cjs:72:    writeFile(skillDir, 'leaf-scopes.json', `${JSON.stringify({ scopes: [{\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.10.md:65:The block's \"Before you start\" step opens with `bash .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh provision .` for a fresh clone and `git config --local skilled.trustRepoHooks true` for a clone that should run the hooks. The removal steps name the two feature-catalog files and regenerate `graph-metadata.json` with `regenerate-skill-derived.cjs`. The add steps name `leaf-scopes.json` and the surface-count lines the documentation claim checker reads.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/README.md:150:3. Add the packet's paths to the `ROUTER.md` maps and section 8, and its `surfaceDetection` block to its `mode-registry.json` entry (`stack-detection.md` section 2 reads it). Update any surface-count wording that `verify-doc-claims.cjs` checks in the hub's `README.md` and `SKILL.md`. `phase-detection.md` names the surfaces without a count. A packet copied from an existing surface has the same leaf set as that surface, so `generate-leaf-manifest.cjs --write` stops with `MODE_LEAF_SET_COLLISION`. Give each of the two modes its own `leafScopes` in a new `leaf-scopes.json` at the hub root, in the array format `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/leaf-scopes.json` uses, or change the copy until its files differ.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.17.23.0.md:32:- **`hooks/` is Markdown-only through `leaf-scopes.json`.** The scope names its five hook docs, so the nine runtime `.ts`, `.py` and `.json` files beside them are never leaves.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.17.21.0.md:24:- **The `hooks/` leaf root is Markdown only.** Nine non-`.md` files under `hooks/` left the leaf manifest and the alias file, and `leaf-scopes.json` now limits that leaf root to Markdown. No route changed.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:102:- Every routable leaf under the five declared leaf roots, `references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, `manual-testing-playbook/` and `hooks/`, is enumerated in `leaf-manifest.json`, generated from `leaf-manifest.config.json` and narrowed by `leaf-scopes.json`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103:- `hooks/` is Markdown-only through `leaf-scopes.json`: the scope names its five hook docs, and the nine runtime `.ts`, `.py` and `.json` files beside them are never leaves. `assets/` is declared and has no docs to contribute.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.3.0.md:3:description: \"A standalone skill now reads leaf-scopes.json, so it can narrow a configured leaf root to the files its router actually selects. system-skill-advisor is the first to use it, keeping only Markdown under hooks/.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.3.0.md:17:`leaf-scopes.json` already narrowed a hub's mode to its own packet-relative subtrees. The standalone path now reads the same file through the same helpers, so one option serves both kinds of skill and a scope is spelled the same way in either.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.3.0.md:35:No action is needed. A skill with no `leaf-scopes.json`, or with an empty scope list, walks its full leaf roots exactly as before.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:3:description: \"The packet, the root-metadata contract and the standalone playbook now name leaf-scopes.json, the optional authored file that narrows a standalone skill's leaf roots, with the two codes that stop a bad scope.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:16:A standalone skill could author `leaf-scopes.json`, but nothing in this packet said so. The generator had read the file since the standalone scoping release, and `system-skill-advisor` already depends on it to keep `hooks/` Markdown-only, yet an author following the skill met the capability only in a changelog entry.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:26:- **The file is named where an author looks.** The standalone shape lists `leaf-scopes.json` as optional, and the prose says which roots it narrows and why.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.5.0.md:37:No action is needed. A root without `leaf-scopes.json` generates the same manifest it did before.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:71:| `leaf-scopes.json` | optional, authored | optional, authored | authored |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:90:### Why `leaf-scopes.json` is optional for both classes\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:113:Everything else carries authored semantic identity, routing policy, or a declaration only a human can make: `graph-metadata.json`, `description.json`, `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json`, `leaf-manifest.config.json`, `command-metadata.json` and `leaf-scopes.json`, plus `leaf-aliases.json` on a hub, where the projection carries real compatibility mappings rather than a derivative. `--fix` reads every one of them and never rewrites one.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:182:**A new standalone skill (S):** author `SKILL.md`, `graph-metadata.json`, and `leaf-manifest.config.json`, because that config is the single declaration that names the workflow mode and the leaf roots. Add `leaf-scopes.json` only when a configured leaf root must be narrowed to a subtree or a named set of docs. Add `command-metadata.json` only when the skill ships slash commands, and set every entry's `ownerMode` to the skill's own id. Run `--fix` to generate the manifest and the alias projection.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:184:A standalone root therefore needs exactly one required authored metadata file beyond identity. `leaf-scopes.json` and `command-metadata.json` stay optional, added only when the root needs them. That is the whole delta between a non-conforming root and a conforming one.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:188:Every authored file except `leaf-scopes.json` has a scaffold under `sk-create-skill/assets/`. The two generated files deliberately have none, because hand-editing them is what the freshness gate exists to catch. For the scope file, copy the shape from a shipped root. A standalone root reuses the hub scaffold for `command-metadata.json` and sets every entry's `ownerMode` to its own skill id.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:200:| `leaf-scopes.json` | H + S | none — copy a shipped root, such as `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-scopes.json` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:166:Verify that a standalone root authors `graph-metadata.json` and `leaf-manifest.config.json`, adds `leaf-scopes.json` only when a leaf root needs narrowing, omits hub-only declarations and generates fresh manifest files.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:172:The mode should classify the root as class S because it declares neither `mode-registry.json` nor `hub-router.json`. It should author the identity and leaf config, run the metadata gate with `--fix` and confirm that `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` are generated. It should not add `description.json` or a parent registry. When a declared leaf root needs narrowing, it should add `leaf-scopes.json` for the config's single `workflowMode` and confirm that a scope outside the declared roots fails with `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` and a scope on an undeclared mode fails with `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:30:- Expected execution process: inspect the root, confirm it declares neither `mode-registry.json` nor `hub-router.json`, author `graph-metadata.json` and `leaf-manifest.config.json`, add `leaf-scopes.json` only when a declared leaf root needs narrowing, run `ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs --fix`, confirm fresh generated files and prove both bad-scope failures.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:31:- Expected signals: class S is named, `graph-metadata.json` and `leaf-manifest.config.json` are authored, `leaf-scopes.json` is named as the optional authored file that narrows a declared leaf root for the config's single `workflowMode`, `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` are generated and hub-only files are absent. A scope outside the declared leaf roots reports `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` and a scope on an undeclared workflow mode reports `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:45:| SKL-002 | Classify standalone root metadata | Classify a standalone root and produce the correct authored and generated metadata files | `My new skill is standalone. Which root metadata files should I author and which ones should the gate generate?` | 1. `agent: Read the standalone class row in references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` -> 2. `agent: Confirm the root declares neither mode-registry.json nor hub-router.json` -> 3. `agent: Author graph-metadata.json and leaf-manifest.config.json, the required class-S set` -> 4. `agent: When a declared leaf root needs narrowing, add leaf-scopes.json naming the config's workflowMode` -> 5. `bash: node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs --fix` -> 6. `bash: node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs` -> 7. `bash: node --test .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/generate-leaf-manifest-standalone-scopes.test.cjs` | Step 1: class S is named. Step 2: both hub declarations are absent. Step 3: the required authored set is correct and no scope file is invented for a root that needs none. Step 4: the scope stays under a declared leaf root and names the configured `workflowMode`. Step 5: generated manifests are refreshed, and a scoped root's manifest lists only the scoped leaves. Step 6: the final gate is clean. Step 7: the scoped-generator suite passes, which proves `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` stops a scope outside the declared roots and `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE` stops a scope on an undeclared mode | The exact prompt, class row, root metadata listing, both gate transcripts with exit statuses, the scope failure output and the final file ownership map | PASS if the authored and generated sets match class S, any scope stays under a declared leaf root, and the final gate reports clean. FAIL if a hub-only file is present, a scope escapes the declared roots or names an undeclared mode, or generated output is hand-authored | 1. Compare the root files with the class S matrix. 2. Check that `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` match generated output. 3. Re-run the gate without `--fix` and read its exit status. 4. Compare a failing scope's `workflowMode` with `leaf-manifest.config.json` and its path with the declared `leafRoots`, which is what separates `ORPHAN_LEAF_SCOPE_MODE` from `OUT_OF_ROOT_LEAF_SCOPE` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:52:4. `agent: When a declared leaf root needs narrowing, add leaf-scopes.json naming the config's workflowMode`\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:73:2. Compare the root file set with the class S matrix, including whether `leaf-scopes.json` was needed at all.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/manual-testing-playbook/standalone-skill/classify-standalone-root-metadata.md:95:| [`scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs`](../../scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs) | Reads `leaf-scopes.json` and fails closed on a bad scope |\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/generate-leaf-manifest-standalone-scopes.test.cjs:35:    writeFile(skillDir, 'leaf-scopes.json', `${JSON.stringify({ scopes: [{\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/generate-leaf-manifest-standalone-scopes.test.cjs:72:    writeFile(skillDir, 'leaf-scopes.json', `${JSON.stringify({ scopes: [{\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"leaf-scopes.json\\\" --include=*.cjs --include=*.mjs --include=*.ts --include=*.js --include=*.md .skilled | grep -v \\\"leaf-scopes.json:\\\" | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780697757,"end":1794780708864}}}}
