{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780738696,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e144b27e001JHlqy4KpAKDB4f","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14489e5001u1Dt7ZHLIRfWNy","type":"tool","id":"call_47c7cd97dd5a4bcd863eda18","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md","offset":20,"limit":60},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md, lines 20-79\n20: - `operator-h5/`\n21: - `auto-update-daemon/`\n22: - `auto-indexing/`\n23: - `lifecycle-routing/`\n24: - `scorer-fusion/`\n25: - `python-compat/`\n26: \n27: ### Result persistence\n28: \n29: <!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->\n30: A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its reason and its evidence paths are recorded by hand in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. The first recorded run creates that folder, because the wrapper that once wrote these records was retired and no renderer writes them now.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n35: \n36: This playbook provides 53 scenario files across 9 categories, one of them a live conversation scenario, validating the Skill Advisor surface. Scenario IDs use a multi-prefix scheme: `NC` for the native command surface, `CL` for CLI hooks plus plugin behavior, `CP` for compatibility plus disable controls, `OP` for operator H5 states, `AU` for auto-update daemon behavior, `AI` for auto-indexing, `LC` for lifecycle routing, `SC` for scorer fusion and `PC` for Python compatibility.\n37: \n38: Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 53 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n39: \n40: ### Realistic Test Model\n41: \n42: 1. A realistic user request is given to an operator or runtime.\n43: 2. The operator decides whether to call the native command through the CLI, run a prompt-time hook, execute compatibility shims or inspect daemon/indexing behavior.\n44: 3. The operator captures command transcripts, CLI JSON envelopes, hook stdout/stderr and final verdicts.\n45: 4. The scenario passes only when observed output is prompt-safe, user-visible and consistent with the documented feature contract.\n46: \n47: ### What Each Feature File Should Explain\n48: \n49: - The realistic user request or operational state that should trigger the behavior.\n50: - The deterministic setup and execution steps.\n51: - The expected signals and failure modes.\n52: - The desired user-visible outcome.\n53: - The implementation, automated test or catalog anchors that justify the scenario.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 2. GLOBAL PRECONDITIONS\n58: \n59: 1. Working directory is the repository root.\n60: 2. Node.js and Python 3 are available.\n61: 3. The advisor runtime build is current:\n62: \n63: ```bash\n64: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n65: ```\n66: \n67: 4. `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` is unset unless a scenario explicitly sets it.\n68: 5. Operators can run the documented advisor CLI and Node/Python commands from the repo root.\n69: 6. Destructive or stateful scenarios use a disposable workspace copy unless the scenario explicitly validates the live checkout.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 3. GLOBAL EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS\n74: \n75: - Scenario ID and per-feature file path.\n76: - User request or operational condition used.\n77: - Exact command transcript or CLI call payload.\n78: - Full JSON output or a focused excerpt containing asserted fields.\n79: - Exit code for shell commands.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 80]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md, lines 20-79\n20: - `operator-h5/`\n21: - `auto-update-daemon/`\n22: - `auto-indexing/`\n23: - `lifecycle-routing/`\n24: - `scorer-fusion/`\n25: - `python-compat/`\n26: \n27: ### Result persistence\n28: \n29: <!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->\n30: A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its reason and its evidence paths are recorded by hand in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. The first recorded run creates that folder, because the wrapper that once wrote these records was retired and no renderer writes them now.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n35: \n36: This playbook provides 53 scenario files across 9 categories, one of them a live conversation scenario, validating the Skill Advisor surface. Scenario IDs use a multi-prefix scheme: `NC` for the native command surface, `CL` for CLI hooks plus plugin behavior, `CP` for compatibility plus disable controls, `OP` for operator H5 states, `AU` for auto-update daemon behavior, `AI` for auto-indexing, `LC` for lifecycle routing, `SC` for scorer fusion and `PC` for Python compatibility.\n37: \n38: Coverage note (2026-05-07): the prior operator scenario corpus now lives under `manual-testing-playbook/` as the canonical manual validation package. Former `SAD-NNN` IDs are deprecated plus mapped to current feature files in section 18. The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 53 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`. This root playbook reflects the live file inventory.\n39: \n40: ### Realistic Test Model\n41: \n42: 1. A realistic user request is given to an operator or runtime.\n43: 2. The operator decides whether to call the native command through the CLI, run a prompt-time hook, execute compatibility shims or inspect daemon/indexing behavior.\n44: 3. The operator captures command transcripts, CLI JSON envelopes, hook stdout/stderr and final verdicts.\n45: 4. The scenario passes only when observed output is prompt-safe, user-visible and consistent with the documented feature contract.\n46: \n47: ### What Each Feature File Should Explain\n48: \n49: - The realistic user request or operational state that should trigger the behavior.\n50: - The deterministic setup and execution steps.\n51: - The expected signals and failure modes.\n52: - The desired user-visible outcome.\n53: - The implementation, automated test or catalog anchors that justify the scenario.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 2. GLOBAL PRECONDITIONS\n58: \n59: 1. Working directory is the repository root.\n60: 2. Node.js and Python 3 are available.\n61: 3. The advisor runtime build is current:\n62: \n63: ```bash\n64: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n65: ```\n66: \n67: 4. `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` is unset unless a scenario explicitly sets it.\n68: 5. Operators can run the documented advisor CLI and Node/Python commands from the repo root.\n69: 6. Destructive or stateful scenarios use a disposable workspace copy unless the scenario explicitly validates the live checkout.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 3. GLOBAL EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS\n74: \n75: - Scenario ID and per-feature file path.\n76: - User request or operational condition used.\n77: - Exact command transcript or CLI call payload.\n78: - Full JSON output or a focused excerpt containing asserted fields.\n79: - Exit code for shell commands.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 80]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\",\"offset\":20,