{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780784035,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1455f58001bdQvE7s3pSIZmg","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e1453f97001CTXPy6jfPoBLFS","type":"tool","id":"call_b0df0312a42549c788791f31","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '2230,2290p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs"},"output":"    unscored: tally.unscored,\n    unscoredRuns: tally.unscoredRuns,\n    startRate: rate(tally.started, tally.startRows),\n    cappedStartRows: tally.cappedStartRows,\n    offered: tally.offered,\n    cappedOfferRows: tally.cappedOfferRows,\n    startedOfOffered: tally.startedOfOffered,\n    offerFieldAbsent: tally.offerFieldAbsent,\n    offeredAsPartner: tally.offeredAsPartner,\n    offerReached: tally.offerReached,\n    deliveryUnknown: tally.deliveryUnknown,\n    offerSeen: tally.offerSeen,\n    offerDeclined: tally.offerDeclined,\n    commandLineRate: rate(tally.commandLineRuns, tally.scored),\n    unsafe: tally.unsafe,\n    unsafeNoChangedPath: tally.unsafeNoChangedPath,\n    repeatedCommandLines: tally.repeatedCommandLines,\n    loopsWithoutInit: tally.loopsWithoutInit,\n    loops: tally.loops,\n    workflow: {\n      command: tally.workflow.command,\n      skill: tally.workflow.skill,\n      asked: tally.workflow.asked,\n      askedActed: tally.workflow.askedActed,\n      otherMode: tally.workflow.otherMode,\n      improvised: tally.workflow.improvised,\n      none: tally.workflow.none,\n      noneActed: tally.workflow.noneActed,\n      noOwner: tally.workflow.noOwner,\n      unscored: tally.unscored,\n      // The load rate is the outcome reading: every owned run the arm scored is in\n      // its denominator, so a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot\n      // leave the count the way it leaves the share.\n      loadRate: rate(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked + tally.workflow.otherMode + tally.workflow.improvised + tally.workflow.none,\n      ),\n      followedRate: rate(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked + tally.workflow.otherMode + tally.workflow.improvised + tally.workflow.none,\n      ),\n      // The same followed counts are read again within each group the offer puts a run\n      // in, because a run the head never offered the command to cannot follow that offer.\n      followedOffered: rate(\n        tally.followedByOffer.offered.followed,\n        tally.followedByOffer.offered.total,\n      ),\n      followedNotOffered: rate(\n        tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.followed,\n        tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.total,\n      ),\n      offerUnknown: tally.followedByOffer.unknown,\n      share: rate(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.improvised,\n      ),\n      // The rate keeps its text and the interval sits beside it, so a reader can tell\n      // a clean arm from a large one without parsing the counts back out.\n      followedRange: wilsonRange(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked + tally.workflow.otherMode + tally.workflow.improvised + tally.workflow.none,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    unscored: tally.unscored,\n    unscoredRuns: tally.unscoredRuns,\n    startRate: rate(tally.started, tally.startRows),\n    cappedStartRows: tally.cappedStartRows,\n    offered: tally.offered,\n    cappedOfferRows: tally.cappedOfferRows,\n    startedOfOffered: tally.startedOfOffered,\n    offerFieldAbsent: tally.offerFieldAbsent,\n    offeredAsPartner: tally.offeredAsPartner,\n    offerReached: tally.offerReached,\n    deliveryUnknown: tally.deliveryUnknown,\n    offerSeen: tally.offerSeen,\n    offerDeclined: tally.offerDeclined,\n    commandLineRate: rate(tally.commandLineRuns, tally.scored),\n    unsafe: tally.unsafe,\n    unsafeNoChangedPath: tally.unsafeNoChangedPath,\n    repeatedCommandLines: tally.repeatedCommandLines,\n    loopsWithoutInit: tally.loopsWithoutInit,\n    loops: tally.loops,\n    workflow: {\n      command: tally.workflow.command,\n      skill: tally.workflow.skill,\n      asked: tally.workflow.asked,\n      askedActed: tally.workflow.askedActed,\n      otherMode: tally.workflow.otherMode,\n      improvised: tally.workflow.improvised,\n      none: tally.workflow.none,\n      noneActed: tally.workflow.noneActed,\n      noOwner: tally.workflow.noOwner,\n      unscored: tally.unscored,\n      // The load rate is the outcome reading: every owned run the arm scored is in\n      // its denominator, so a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot\n      // leave the count the way it leaves the share.\n      loadRate: rate(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked + tally.workflow.otherMode + tally.workflow.improvised + tally.workflow.none,\n      ),\n      followedRate: rate(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked + tally.workflow.otherMode + tally.workflow.improvised + tally.workflow.none,\n      ),\n      // The same followed counts are read again within each group the offer puts a run\n      // in, because a run the head never offered the command to cannot follow that offer.\n      followedOffered: rate(\n        tally.followedByOffer.offered.followed,\n        tally.followedByOffer.offered.total,\n      ),\n      followedNotOffered: rate(\n        tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.followed,\n        tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.total,\n      ),\n      offerUnknown: tally.followedByOffer.unknown,\n      share: rate(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.improvised,\n      ),\n      // The rate keeps its text and the interval sits beside it, so a reader can tell\n      // a clean arm from a large one without parsing the counts back out.\n      followedRange: wilsonRange(\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked,\n        tally.workflow.command + tally.workflow.skill + tally.workflow.asked + tally.workflow.otherMode + tally.workflow.improvised + tally.workflow.none,\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '2230,2290p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780782424,"end":1794780784035}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780784044,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14561a2001QsWisGN7c5kbmS","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e1453f97001CTXPy6jfPoBLFS","type":"tool","id":"call_653923dac138493399cad2e8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .skilled/commands/create/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== changelog 100-115 and 200-212 ===\"; sed -n '100,112p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; echo \"---\"; sed -n '200,212p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md"},"output":"agent.md\nassets\nbenchmark.md\nchangelog.md\ncommand.md\ndiff.md\nfeature-catalog.md\ngoal.md\nmanual-testing-playbook.md\nreadme.md\nREADME.txt\nrepo-rule.md\nsk-skill.md\nskill-parent.md\nwith-human-voice.md\n=== changelog 100-115 and 200-212 ===\n#### A Mode Suffix Still Counts\n\nA command typed with its mode suffix reads as that command. So `/deep:review:auto` attaches `/deep:review`. The suffixes are `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot`. Any other suffix reads as no command.\n\n#### The Retired Create-Skill Name Still Reads\n\nA typed `/create:skill` now reads as `/create:sk-skill`. So a prompt that types the old name gets `sk-doc` with `/create:sk-skill (start)`. No command file answers to the old name. The retired name lives only in the `RETIRED_COMMANDS` table in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`. `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` covers it. A path such as `docs/create:skill.md` still reads as no command.\n\n#### The Doctor Helper for Missing Tools\n\nA prompt that says a tool does not show up now counts as a strong problem cue. The same holds when a tool does not appear. The brief then adds `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. \"Appear to\" and \"up-to-date\" stay out of the cue. A contraction typed with a curly apostrophe counts like a straight one.\n\n#### A Weak Cue Beside a Words-Only Skill\n---\n&nbsp;\n\n## Renamed Command\n\n#### The Create-Skill Row Has a New Id\n\n**Breaking:** The command row `command-create-skill` is now `command-create-sk-skill`. Its slash markers are now `/create:sk-skill`. A typed `/create:skill` reads as `/create:sk-skill`, as Brief Commands above says. The rename itself is in the `sk-doc` v2.10.0.0 entry.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## OpenCode Plugin\n\n#### One Head Line in the Brief\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"agent.md\nassets\nbenchmark.md\nchangelog.md\ncommand.md\ndiff.md\nfeature-catalog.md\ngoal.md\nmanual-testing-playbook.md\nreadme.md\nREADME.txt\nrepo-rule.md\nsk-skill.md\nskill-parent.md\nwith-human-voice.md\n=== changelog 100-115 and 200-212 ===\n#### A Mode Suffix Still Counts\n\nA command typed with its mode suffix reads as that command. So `/deep:review:auto` attaches `/deep:review`. The suffixes are `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot`. Any other suffix reads as no command.\n\n#### The Retired Create-Skill Name Still Reads\n\nA typed `/create:skill` now reads as `/create:sk-skill`. So a prompt that types the old name gets `sk-doc` with `/create:sk-skill (start)`. No command file answers to the old name. The retired name lives only in the `RETIRED_COMMANDS` table in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`. `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` covers it. A path such as `docs/create:skill.md` still reads as no command.\n\n#### The Doctor Helper for Missing Tools\n\nA prompt that says a tool does not show up now counts as a strong problem cue. The same holds when a tool does not appear. The brief then adds `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. \"Appear to\" and \"up-to-date\" stay out of the cue. A contraction typed with a curly apostrophe counts like a straight one.\n\n#### A Weak Cue Beside a Words-Only Skill\n---\n&nbsp;\n\n## Renamed Command\n\n#### The Create-Skill Row Has a New Id\n\n**Breaking:** The command row `command-create-skill` is now `command-create-sk-skill`. Its slash markers are now `/create:sk-skill`. A typed `/create:skill` reads as `/create:sk-skill`, as Brief Commands above says. The rename itself is in the `sk-doc` v2.10.0.0 entry.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## OpenCode Plugin\n\n#### One Head Line in the Brief\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .skilled/commands/create/ 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"=== changelog 100-115 and 200-212 ===\\\"; sed -n '100,112p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; echo \\\"---\\\"; sed -n '200,212p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780783010,"end":1794780784044}}}}
