{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780826902,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1460ba4001J6LMA8RxUuwaWQ","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e145c3ff00173jPjhoWUnhdlI","type":"tool","id":"call_9ef5bbc25ab64587a6d51c6e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md","limit":95},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md, lines 1-95\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\"\n3: description: \"Vitest, Python and fixture coverage for skill-advisor routing, handlers, hooks, schemas, scorer paths and compatibility behavior.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor tests\"\n6:   - \"advisor regression tests\"\n7:   - \"skill advisor vitest\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime/tests/` is the regression surface for the skill-advisor package. It groups focused Vitest suites, compatibility checks, handler and hook tests, schema checks, Python parity tests and shared fixtures used by the advisor scorer and daemon paths.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Covers advisor routing, scorer, lane attribution, cache, daemon freshness and lifecycle metadata behavior.\n21: - Keeps compatibility, parity and schema tests in named subfolders.\n22: - Provides shared fixtures and helpers used across direct TypeScript and Python-facing advisor checks.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n27: \n28: ```text\n29: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n30: │                      SKILL ADVISOR TESTS                         │\n31: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n32: \n33: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n34: │ Test runner  │ ───▶ │ Vitest suites   │ ───▶ │ Advisor modules  │\n35: │ npm / vitest │      │ tests/*.ts      │      │ lib / handlers   │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                      │                        │\n38:        │                      ▼                        ▼\n39:        │              ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────┐\n40:        └───────────▶  │ Fixtures      │ ───▶   │ Schemas        │\n41:                       │ tests/fixtures│        │ schemas/*      │\n42:                       └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n43:                               │\n44:                               ▼\n45:                       ┌───────────────┐\n46:                       │ Python parity │\n47:                       └───────────────┘\n48: \n49: Dependency direction: test suites -> fixtures -> advisor runtime modules\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n55: \n56: ```text\n57: tests/\n58: +-- cache/                   # Cache behavior coverage\n59: +-- compat/                  # Compatibility contract checks\n60: +-- fixtures/                # Prompt, graph and routing fixtures\n61: +-- helpers/                 # Test-only helpers (env snapshot, activation-matrix evidence)\n62: +-- handlers/                # Handler tests\n63: +-- hooks/                   # Hook integration tests\n64: +-- legacy/                  # Legacy compatibility coverage\n65: +-- parity/                  # Cross-runtime parity checks\n66: +-- python/                  # Python wrapper and script tests\n67: +-- schemas/                 # Schema validation tests\n68: +-- scorer/                  # Native scorer tests\n69: +-- embedders/               # Embedder schema and shared parity tests\n70: +-- skill-graph/             # Skill-graph round-trip tests\n71: +-- *.vitest.ts              # Package-level regression suites\n72: +-- *.test.ts                # Focused unit tests\n73: `-- README.md\n74: ```\n75: \n76: Allowed direction:\n77: \n78: ```text\n79: tests -> fixtures\n80: tests -> skill_advisor/lib\n81: tests -> skill_advisor/handlers\n82: ```\n83: \n84: Disallowed direction:\n85: \n86: ```text\n87: runtime code -> tests\n88: fixtures -> generated runtime state without an explicit test setup\n89: ```\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n94: \n95: ```text\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 96]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md, lines 1-95\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\"\n3: description: \"Vitest, Python and fixture coverage for skill-advisor routing, handlers, hooks, schemas, scorer paths and compatibility behavior.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor tests\"\n6:   - \"advisor regression tests\"\n7:   - \"skill advisor vitest\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime/tests/` is the regression surface for the skill-advisor package. It groups focused Vitest suites, compatibility checks, handler and hook tests, schema checks, Python parity tests and shared fixtures used by the advisor scorer and daemon paths.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Covers advisor routing, scorer, lane attribution, cache, daemon freshness and lifecycle metadata behavior.\n21: - Keeps compatibility, parity and schema tests in named subfolders.\n22: - Provides shared fixtures and helpers used across direct TypeScript and Python-facing advisor checks.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n27: \n28: ```text\n29: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n30: │                      SKILL ADVISOR TESTS                         │\n31: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n32: \n33: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n34: │ Test runner  │ ───▶ │ Vitest suites   │ ───▶ │ Advisor modules  │\n35: │ npm / vitest │      │ tests/*.ts      │      │ lib / handlers   │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                      │                        │\n38:        │                      ▼                        ▼\n39:        │              ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────┐\n40:        └───────────▶  │ Fixtures      │ ───▶   │ Schemas        │\n41:                       │ tests/fixtures│        │ schemas/*      │\n42:                       └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n43:                               │\n44:                               ▼\n45:                       ┌───────────────┐\n46:                       │ Python parity │\n47:                       └───────────────┘\n48: \n49: Dependency direction: test suites -> fixtures -> advisor runtime modules\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n55: \n56: ```text\n57: tests/\n58: +-- cache/                   # Cache behavior coverage\n59: +-- compat/                  # Compatibility contract checks\n60: +-- fixtures/                # Prompt, graph and routing fixtures\n61: +-- helpers/                 # Test-only helpers (env snapshot, activation-matrix evidence)\n62: +-- handlers/                # Handler tests\n63: +-- hooks/                   # Hook integration tests\n64: +-- legacy/                  # Legacy compatibility coverage\n65: +-- parity/                  # Cross-runtime parity checks\n66: +-- python/                  # Python wrapper and script tests\n67: +-- schemas/                 # Schema validation tests\n68: +-- scorer/                  # Native scorer tests\n69: +-- embedders/               # Embedder schema and shared parity tests\n70: +-- skill-graph/             # Skill-graph round-trip tests\n71: +-- *.vitest.ts              # Package-level regression suites\n72: +-- *.test.ts                # Focused unit tests\n73: `-- README.md\n74: ```\n75: \n76: Allowed direction:\n77: \n78: ```text\n79: tests -> fixtures\n80: tests -> skill_advisor/lib\n81: tests -> skill_advisor/handlers\n82: ```\n83: \n84: Disallowed direction:\n85: \n86: ```text\n87: runtime code -> tests\n88: fixtures -> generated runtime state without an explicit test setup\n89: ```\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n94: \n95: ```text\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 96]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\",\"limit\":95}"},"time":{"start":1794780826532,"end":1794780826902}}}}
