{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780834108,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1462773001NIZHAHalq4aQmd","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e146117d001Qqbm051yEQFWNy","type":"tool","id":"call_95fcf8a87b87406fae997efa","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md","offset":205,"limit":120},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md, lines 205-278\n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 5. KEY FILES\n208: \n209: | File | Responsibility |\n210: |---|---|\n211: | `lane-attribution.test.ts` | Verifies prompt-safe lane attribution behavior. |\n212: | `affordance-normalizer.test.ts` | Tests affordance normalization used by advisor routing. |\n213: | `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n214: | `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n215: | `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n216: | `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |\n217: | `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n218: | `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n219: | `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 28 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, a meaning pass must also clear the uncertainty bar, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n220: | `command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` | Pins the `derivePolicy` ladder and the closed risk-key vocabularies, and checks that the command tree and its declarations agree. |\n221: | `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Holds live command routing to `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` row by row, pins the corpus hash and requires a typed row and both plain splits for every command file. |\n222: | `embedders/` | Covers embedder schema, registry and shared-factory parity. |\n223: | `skill-graph/` | Covers focused skill-graph refresh round trips. |\n224: | `tsconfig.tests.json` | Type-checks the CLI and launcher test files listed in its `include`, extending the runtime `tsconfig.json`, with no emit. |\n225: \n226: ---\n227: \n228: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n229: \n230: | Boundary | Rule |\n231: |---|---|\n232: | Imports | Tests may import advisor runtime modules, schemas, fixtures and local shared helpers. |\n233: | Exports | This folder exports no production runtime code. |\n234: | Ownership | Keep advisor package tests here. Put code-graph, memory or deep-loop tests in their own package folders. |\n235: \n236: Main flow:\n237: \n238: ```text\n239: fixture or inline scenario\n240:   -> advisor scorer, handler, hook or schema path\n241:   -> prompt-safe result, metadata or validation output\n242:   -> assertion on stable advisor behavior\n243: ```\n244: \n245: ---\n246: \n247: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n248: \n249: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n250: |---|---|---|\n251: | `*.vitest.ts` | Test files | Vitest regression suites for daemon, lifecycle, shadow and database behavior. |\n252: | `*.test.ts` | Test files | Focused unit tests for affordance and attribution helpers. |\n253: | `fixtures/` | Test data | Shared prompt and routing inputs. |\n254: | `scorer/` | Test folder | Native scorer regression coverage. |\n255: | `embedders/` | Test folder | Embedder boundary and schema coverage. |\n256: | `skill-graph/` | Test folder | Focused skill-graph database coverage. |\n257: \n258: ---\n259: \n260: ## 8. VALIDATION\n261: \n262: Run from the repository root.\n263: \n264: ```bash\n265: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\n266: ```\n267: \n268: Expected result: exit code `0`.\n269: \n270: ---\n271: \n272: ## 9. RELATED\n273: \n274: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n275: - [`../lib/README.md`](../lib/README.md)\n276: - [`embedders/README.md`](embedders/README.md)\n277: - [`skill-graph/README.md`](skill-graph/README.md)\n278: - [`scorer/README.md`](scorer/README.md)","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md, lines 205-278\n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 5. KEY FILES\n208: \n209: | File | Responsibility |\n210: |---|---|\n211: | `lane-attribution.test.ts` | Verifies prompt-safe lane attribution behavior. |\n212: | `affordance-normalizer.test.ts` | Tests affordance normalization used by advisor routing. |\n213: | `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n214: | `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n215: | `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n216: | `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |\n217: | `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n218: | `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n219: | `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 28 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, a meaning pass must also clear the uncertainty bar, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n220: | `command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` | Pins the `derivePolicy` ladder and the closed risk-key vocabularies, and checks that the command tree and its declarations agree. |\n221: | `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Holds live command routing to `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` row by row, pins the corpus hash and requires a typed row and both plain splits for every command file. |\n222: | `embedders/` | Covers embedder schema, registry and shared-factory parity. |\n223: | `skill-graph/` | Covers focused skill-graph refresh round trips. |\n224: | `tsconfig.tests.json` | Type-checks the CLI and launcher test files listed in its `include`, extending the runtime `tsconfig.json`, with no emit. |\n225: \n226: ---\n227: \n228: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n229: \n230: | Boundary | Rule |\n231: |---|---|\n232: | Imports | Tests may import advisor runtime modules, schemas, fixtures and local shared helpers. |\n233: | Exports | This folder exports no production runtime code. |\n234: | Ownership | Keep advisor package tests here. Put code-graph, memory or deep-loop tests in their own package folders. |\n235: \n236: Main flow:\n237: \n238: ```text\n239: fixture or inline scenario\n240:   -> advisor scorer, handler, hook or schema path\n241:   -> prompt-safe result, metadata or validation output\n242:   -> assertion on stable advisor behavior\n243: ```\n244: \n245: ---\n246: \n247: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n248: \n249: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n250: |---|---|---|\n251: | `*.vitest.ts` | Test files | Vitest regression suites for daemon, lifecycle, shadow and database behavior. |\n252: | `*.test.ts` | Test files | Focused unit tests for affordance and attribution helpers. |\n253: | `fixtures/` | Test data | Shared prompt and routing inputs. |\n254: | `scorer/` | Test folder | Native scorer regression coverage. |\n255: | `embedders/` | Test folder | Embedder boundary and schema coverage. |\n256: | `skill-graph/` | Test folder | Focused skill-graph database coverage. |\n257: \n258: ---\n259: \n260: ## 8. VALIDATION\n261: \n262: Run from the repository root.\n263: \n264: ```bash\n265: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\n266: ```\n267: \n268: Expected result: exit code `0`.\n269: \n270: ---\n271: \n272: ## 9. RELATED\n273: \n274: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n275: - [`../lib/README.md`](../lib/README.md)\n276: - [`embedders/README.md`](embedders/README.md)\n277: - [`skill-graph/README.md`](skill-graph/README.md)\n278: - [`scorer/README.md`](scorer/README.md)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\",\"offset\":205,\"limit\":120}"},"time":{"start":1794780833651,"end":1794780834108}}}}
