{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780888203,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e146f81e00155G4JYumXIZ3Iq","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14695fc001eNBVh2IG7dYHMH","type":"tool","id":"call_2fc63c638a6f473cb30951e7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"hooks/\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md | head -30; echo \"=== RESOURCE_MAP ===\"; grep -n \"RESOURCE_MAP\" -A 40 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md | head -60"},"output":"34:- **Hooks:** `hooks/` for prompt-time hook behavior.\n55:- **HOOK** — fires on \"skill advisor hook\", \"prompt-time hook\", \"pi prompt advisor\", \"prompt-time brief\", \"advisor skipped my prompt\", \"advisor skip my prompt\", \"userpromptsubmit\", \"opencode plugin bridge\", \"goal opencode plugin\"; loads `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n94:- `hooks/` documents prompt-time hook behavior across runtimes.\n102:- Every routable leaf under the five declared leaf roots, `references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, `manual-testing-playbook/` and `hooks/`, is enumerated in `leaf-manifest.json`, generated from `leaf-manifest.config.json` and narrowed by `leaf-scopes.json`.\n103:- `hooks/` is Markdown-only through `leaf-scopes.json`: the scope names its five hook docs, and the nine runtime `.ts`, `.py` and `.json` files beside them are never leaves. `assets/` is declared and has no docs to contribute.\n217:    \"HOOK\": [\"hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\"],\n=== RESOURCE_MAP ===\n107:- The `RESOURCE_MAP` below emits those exact leaf paths.\n108-- The feature-catalog and manual-testing-playbook package indexes are navigation only. They are never routed as typed leaves.\n109-- Do not hand-edit either generated file.\n110-- The `runtime/` advisor engine (`skill-graph.json`, scorer/prompt-policy config, handlers) is the runtime, not a routable documentation leaf. It is intentionally outside every `leafRoot` and never appears in the manifest.\n111-\n112-### Resource loading levels\n113-\n114-| Level | When to Load | Resources |\n115-|---|---|---|\n116-| FALLBACK | Request too weak to score | The two `DEFAULT_RESOURCES` runtime references, offered with the disambiguation checklist (fallback-only: never unioned into a scored route) |\n117:| SELECTED | An intent scores | The exact `RESOURCE_MAP[intent]` leaf(s) for the selected intent(s), emitted as typed `(WORKFLOW_MODE, leafResourceId)` pairs |\n118-| NAVIGATION | Broad \"list the features / playbook\" browse | A `PACKAGE_INDEXES` index doc: navigation only, never a typed leaf |\n119-\n120-### Smart router pseudocode\n121-\n122-The prompt-time brief can show a runnable `/doctor:` command as the top line or as an `Also:` second line under a skill.\n123-\n124-This pseudocode is the canonical resource-routing contract. The router is a singleton-mode selector:\n125-\n126-- It scores the request against `INTENT_SIGNALS`.\n127-- It keeps the intents within the ambiguity delta of the top score, at most two.\n128:- It resolves each intent to its exact `RESOURCE_MAP` leaf path. Use no directory prefixes, filename stems or globs.\n129-- Every selected leaf projects to a typed `(WORKFLOW_MODE, leafResourceId)` pair against `leaf-manifest.json` via `leaf-aliases.json`.\n130-- Package indexes and fallback defaults ride their own channels. They never become typed leaves.\n131-- The live advisor scorer, not this router, remains authoritative for runtime skill scoring. See [`references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md`](./references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md).\n132-\n133-```python\n134-from pathlib import Path\n135-\n136-SKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n137-RESOURCE_BASES = (\n138-    SKILL_ROOT / \"references\",\n139-    SKILL_ROOT / \"assets\",\n140-    SKILL_ROOT / \"feature-catalog\",\n141-    SKILL_ROOT / \"manual-testing-playbook\",\n142-    SKILL_ROOT / \"hooks\",\n143-)\n144-\n145-# This standalone skill emits exactly one workflow mode. Every routed leaf is a\n146-# (WORKFLOW_MODE, leafResourceId) pair. leaf-manifest.json is the authorized\n147-# leaf inventory; leaf-aliases.json binds each router-emitted path to its typed\n148-# identity so a deterministic benchmark replay recovers real pairs.\n149-WORKFLOW_MODE = \"system-skill-advisor\"\n150-\n151-# Always-relevant runtime references offered when a request is too weak to\n152-# score. DEFAULT_RESOURCE_SEMANTICS = \"fallback-only\": the defaults are a\n153-# defer-time suggestion surfaced with the disambiguation checklist, never\n154-# unioned into a scored route's typed leaves, so selected-leaf precision holds.\n155-DEFAULT_RESOURCES = [\n156-    \"references/runtime/tool-ids-reference.md\",\n157-    \"references/runtime/standalone-mcp-shape.md\",\n158-]\n159-DEFAULT_RESOURCE_SEMANTICS = \"fallback-only\"\n160-\n161-# Navigation indexes: loadable for browsing, deliberately excluded from typed\n162-# leaves and from leaf-manifest.json. A broad \"list the features / playbook\"\n163-# request loads these; they never become a (mode, leaf) pair.\n164-PACKAGE_INDEXES = {\n165-    \"FEATURES\": \"feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\",\n166-    \"PLAYBOOK\": \"manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"34:- **Hooks:** `hooks/` for prompt-time hook behavior.\n55:- **HOOK** — fires on \"skill advisor hook\", \"prompt-time hook\", \"pi prompt advisor\", \"prompt-time brief\", \"advisor skipped my prompt\", \"advisor skip my prompt\", \"userpromptsubmit\", \"opencode plugin bridge\", \"goal opencode plugin\"; loads `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n94:- `hooks/` documents prompt-time hook behavior across runtimes.\n102:- Every routable leaf under the five declared leaf roots, `references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, `manual-testing-playbook/` and `h