{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780897102,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e147191a001d2Su2cwx27HJpe","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14700bc0013xFRdd2gIn5PCt","type":"tool","id":"call_9ee65faa8de348429ecd15a8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && jq '.modes[0].leaves[]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-manifest.json | wc -l && jq -r '.modes[0].leaves | map(select(startswith(\"hooks/\"))) | length' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-manifest.json && ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/ && git -c core.fsmonitor=false log --oneline -2 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md"},"output":"     120\n6\nprompt-advisor.mjs\nREADME.md\nd75ea735cd5 docs(hooks): name the leaf goal tools and the DSH Git rows in the docs\nf910c17bb5d docs(hooks): add the DSH column and document the adapter layout\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"     120\n6\nprompt-advisor.mjs\nREADME.md\nd75ea735cd5 docs(hooks): name the leaf goal tools and the DSH Git rows in the docs\nf910c17bb5d docs(hooks): add the DSH column and document the adapter layout\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && jq '.modes[0].leaves[]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-manifest.json | wc -l && jq -r '.modes[0].leaves | map(select(startswith(\\\"hooks/\\\"))) | length' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-manifest.json && ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/ && git -c core.fsmonitor=false log --oneline -2 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780895514,"end":1794780897102}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780897163,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14714870017fURcQ6Q24jzGy","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14700bc0013xFRdd2gIn5PCt","type":"tool","id":"call_97df3c3f9172405484bb44a8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"leaf\\b\\|leaves\\|leaf count\\|120\" --include=README.md --include=SKILL.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ | grep -iv \"leaflet\" | head -20; echo \"=== verify-doc-claims advisor ===\"; grep -n \"system-skill-advisor\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/verify-doc-claims.cjs | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/README.md:137:- Schemas with async refinements or transforms can't be compiled, and neither can a few other constructs. That is not an error: `z.compile()` hands the schema back unchanged and it keeps using the regular parser, exactly as global mode leaves it. Pass `{ strict: true }` to throw `ZodCompileAsyncError` / `ZodCompileUnsupportedError` instead.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/safe-buffer/README.md:152:const buf2 = Buffer.from('7468697320697320612074c3a97374', 'hex');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/tinybench/README.md:60:// │    1    │ 'slower task' │  '828'   │ 1207382.7838323202 │ '±7.07%'  │   83    │\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/@jridgewell/sourcemap-codec/README.md:65:amp.js.map - 45120 segments\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:79:- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:111:`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` leaves a `CLAUDE.md` holding `@AGENTS.md` in an arena that has none and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. Before it copies anything it refuses the source with `source_dirty` when a tracked or untracked edit would leave the arena unlike the commit it names, with `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside that folder, and with `symlink_escape` when a link inside a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. It writes the marker as the head, then `source clean`, then one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree and one `tracked-dotenv <path>` line per tracked dotenv file.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. Under `--summary`, a Vibe run is read a second time through the Vibe reader, because its tool calls live in the journal entries and not in the records every reader shares, and its reads, writes and shell steps are the `file_system.read_file`, `file_system.write_file`, `file_system.edit` and `file_system.bash` calls its journal records. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. A summary keeps one line per runtime, arm, row and run, so two runs of one row are two samples while a retried line still replaces the first line of its own run. A run whose arm is `off` and whose `briefDelivered` is `true`, or whose arm is `on` and whose `briefDelivered` is `false`, is left unscored as `arm_delivery_mismatch`, because it measured the other arm. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` points the label reader at another fresh row file, which lets a test label made-up rows before the blind file exists, and no arm or scoring command sets it. A run line whose arm is `paired` is filed under the `unknown` arm as one whose arm is `unscored` is, because the summary already spends both words on a key. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed`, `neitherFollowed` and `unpaired`, to a runtime whose two arms both ran and either of which scored an owned row, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. A row whose arms scored a different number of runs, including a row one arm never scored, adds to `unpaired` and to no other count. `pooled` sums the `paired` blocks of every runtime and holds `from`, `to`, `runtimes`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `ties`, `unpaired` and `p`, where `p` is the exact one-sided sign test over `gained` and `lost`, rounded to four decimals and null when no pair moved either way. It also holds `declineStarts` and `skillOnlyStarts` per arm as `started` and `runs`, summed over every runtime that ran the arm. `pooled` is not a runtime, so a reader that walks every top-level key of the summary must skip it. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy`, `workflow`, `declineStarts`, `skillOnlyStarts` and `commandStartRuns`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A run line stored before the writers kept `offeredAs` holds none, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. A decline or skill-only run started a tracked command when a skill call named it, a `COMMAND:` line reported it `started`, the host expanded it, or the run read the command's document and also wrote inside its checkout. A read with no write is a lookup and not a start, and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line is not a read, so `declineStarts` and `skillOnlyStarts` print as `x of y` over those runs and `commandStartRuns` lists each start with its row, run, command and offered command. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/README.md:62:| `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` | Prints one JSON object with the embedder's cost. It reads `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `/api/ps` at `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`, the `ollama serve` and model runner rows of `ps -axo`, 30 query embeddings and five end-to-end `advisor_recommend` calls. It writes, starts and unloads nothing, so the loaded model leaves on Ollama's own idle timer. Exits 2 when `/api/version` does not answer, naming the URL it tried. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:121:When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/README.md:24:The guards patch turns the adapter on with `promptAdvisor: true`. A fan-out leaf gets no brief: the lineage patch inserts a marker row, and the adapter checks it at event time, because the lineage patch applies before the guards row exists.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md:59:For local documentation, load the leaf mapped to the detected intent.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md:219:  Its `create-skill` packet also owns the [skill-root metadata contract](../sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md), [graph-metadata template](../sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-graph-metadata-template.json) and [leaf-manifest config template](../sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-leaf-manifest-config-template.json) used by this root.\n=== verify-doc-claims advisor ===\ngrep: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/verify-doc-claims.cjs: No such file or directory\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/README.md:137:- Schemas with async refinements or transforms can't be compiled, and neither can a few other constructs. That is not an error: `z.compile()` hands the schema back unchanged and it keeps using the regular parser, exactly as global mode leaves it. Pass `{ strict: true }` to throw `ZodCompileAsyncError` / `ZodCompileUnsupportedError` instead.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/safe-buffer/README.md:152:const buf2 = Buffer.from('7468697320697320612074c3a97374', 'hex');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/tinybench/README.md:60:// │    1    │ 'slower task' │  '828'   │ 1207382.7838323202 │ '±7.07%'  │   83    │\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/@jridgewell/sourcemap-codec/README.md:65:amp.js.map - 45120 segments\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:79:- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:111:`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` leaves a `CLAUDE.md` holding `@AGENTS.md` in an arena that has none and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. Before it copies anything it refuses the source with `source_dirty` when a tracked or untracked edit would leave the arena unlike the commit it names, with `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older t