{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780922823,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1477ff7001OtA9vXVaaWe2fa","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e1474a7a001tNIceRLGRx2MID","type":"tool","id":"call_ac97d9dc059e4f35ad76361e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"loadRate\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; grep -n \"no command file\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; sed -n '170,180p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md"},"output":"176:The transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the `command` and `skill` runs over every owned run. An `otherMode` run sits in its denominator only. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n251:- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no command file. A typed `/create:skill` still reads as `/create:sk-skill`.\n&nbsp;\n\n## Workflow Measure\n\n#### Six Paths and Two Rates\n\nThe transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the `command` and `skill` runs over every owned run. An `otherMode` run sits in its denominator only. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n\n#### Every Shape a Load Takes\n\nA load is a read tool, a skill tool or a shell read. The shell readers include `cat`, `sed -n` and `head`. An in-place `sed` is not a read. A `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror counts too. On Codex, one `exec_command` body counts as one shell step.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"176:The transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the `command` and `skill` runs over every owned run. An `otherMode` run sits in its denominator only. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n251:- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no command file. A typed `/create:skill` still reads as `/create:sk-skill`.\n&nbsp;\n\n## Workflow Measure\n\n#### Six Paths and Two Rates\n\nThe transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the `command` and `skill` runs over every owned run. An `otherMode` run sits in its denominator only. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n\n#### Every Shape a Load Takes\n\nA load is a read tool, a skill tool or a shell read. The shell readers include `cat`, `sed -n` and `head`. An in-place `sed` is not a read. A `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror counts too. On Codex, one `exec_command` body counts as one shell step.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"loadRate\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; grep -n \\\"no command file\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; sed -n '170,180p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780921847,"end":1794780922823}}}}
