{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781003685,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e148b78f001b0puPthqrdAZ4Q","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e148981b00116es6QnFtJMdKt","type":"tool","id":"call_8d1edd410a774a9cb065c465","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"\\b46\\b\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -20; echo \"=== 47 ===\"; grep -rn \"\\b47\\b\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20:The catalog covers 46 features across 7 groups. Group 01 owns daemon correctness. Groups 02-03 own the index and lifecycle surface that feeds the scorer. Group 04 owns scoring. Group 06 owns the command surface: the nine CLI commands plus the stable compat entrypoint. Groups 07-08 cover runtime integrations, OpenCode plugins and Python compatibility.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-rebuild.md:38:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-rebuild.ts:46-101` | Handler core | Reads status, skips live non-forced rebuilds, indexes skills, publishes generation and returns before/after diagnostics |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-status.md:50:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-rebuild.ts:46-51` | Handler | Source reference |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/sweep-reports/seeded-corpus-evaluation-sweep/research/sweep-results.md:9:- promptEmbeddings: 46\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/sweep-reports/hard-intent-corpus-resweep/research/sweep-results-harder.md:9:- promptEmbeddings: 46\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/operator-h5/unavailable-daemon.md:112:46: ```\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== 47 ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26:`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 47 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:230:| Route lookup for every hub | 251.21 ms | 450.47 ms |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/operator-h5/unavailable-daemon.md:113:47: \n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/scorer-fusion/lane-attribution.md:92:      \"checkedAt\": \"2026-07-03T02:35:47.275Z\",\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-validate-slices.md:288:    \"generatedAt\": \"2026-07-03T01:50:47.688Z\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/python-compat/regression-suite.md:74:| Fewer than 47 cases | Dataset loaded partial | Verify JSONL integrity. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20:The catalog covers 46 features across 7 groups. Group 01 owns daemon correctness. Groups 02-03 own the index and lifecycle surface that feeds the scorer. Group 04 owns scoring. Group 06 owns the command surface: the nine CLI commands plus the stable compat entrypoint. Groups 07-08 cover runtime integrations, OpenCode plugins and Python compatibility.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-rebuild.md:38:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-rebuild.ts:46-101` | Handler core | Reads status, skips live non-forced rebuilds, indexes skills, publishes generation and returns before/after diagnostics |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-status.md:50:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-rebuild.ts:46-51` | Handler | Source reference |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/sweep-reports/seeded-corpus-evaluation-sweep/research/sweep-results.md:9:- promptEmbeddings: 46\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/sweep-reports/hard-intent-corpus-resweep/research/sweep-results-harder.md:9:- promptEmbeddings: 46\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/operator-h5/unavailable-daemon.md:112:46: ```\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== 47 ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26:`derive-command-bridges.cjs` writes an `embeddingText` for each command row the TypeScript scorer serves, 47 rows in all. A metadata row leads with its `userIntent.job` sentence and adds its owned phrases. The `description` stands in only when the record states no job. A doctor row uses its router's frontmatter `description` and the route's trigger phrases. Slash command strings are stripped from the text.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:230:| Route lookup for every hub | 251.21 ms | 450.47 ms |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/operator-h5/unavailable-daemon.md:113:47: \n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/scorer-fusion/lane-attribution.md:92:      \"checkedAt\": \"2026-07-03T02:35:47.275Z\",\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-validate-slices.md:288:    \"generatedAt\": \"2026-07-03T01:50:47.688Z\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/python-compat/regression-suite.md:74:| Fewer than 47 cases | Dataset loaded partial | Verify JSONL integrity. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"\\\\b46\\\\b\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -20; echo \\\"=== 47 ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"\\\\b47\\\\b\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781001615,"end":1794781003685}}}}
