{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781020040,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e148fafa001WM41zNpibPdB2g","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e148c47c001VTRGp5IB4Kyr9D","type":"tool","id":"call_e5de128879cc4bcbbf80e907","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 2a1a42263cc:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | sed -n '176p'; echo \"=== README changed in range? ===\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --name-only 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md"},"output":"Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== README changed in range? ===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== README changed in range? ===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 2a1a42263cc:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | sed -n '176p'; echo \\\"=== README changed in range? ===\\\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --name-only 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781018874,"end":1794781020040}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781020096,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e148f770001d0qlf0QrC4MITY","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e148c47c001VTRGp5IB4Kyr9D","type":"tool","id":"call_629732880b6146feb1e672a0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"typescriptActive\\|commandMetadata\\|doctorRoutes\\|pythonActive\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs | head -20; echo \"=== command rows mentions ===\"; grep -rn \"command rows\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -10"},"output":"1363:      commandMetadata: metadata.length,\n1364:      doctorRoutes: doctor.length,\n1366:      typescriptActive: compatibility.typescript.size,\n1367:      pythonActive: compatibility.python.size,\n=== command rows mentions ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:78:- [doctor-command-routing.md](./doctor-command-routing.md) - The phrase anchor that command rows pass on by default.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:101:A paraphrase shares no words with a command's phrases, so it used to reach nothing. Now each of the 45 scored command rows has its own vector. The text behind it is the row's job sentence and its own phrases. Both are written as a person would ask. A doctor row uses its router's description and trigger phrases instead. A skill-graph scan stores these vectors in their own table, beside the skill vectors.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md:48:The meaning anchor for command rows in `fusion.ts` is tested one level up, in `../command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:219:| `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 28 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, a meaning pass must also clear the uncertainty bar, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:137:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. The `off` and `on` arms compare one commit with the advisor switched off and on, where a turn under either drops every inherited name that ends `_DISABLED` and holds `SKILL_ADVISOR` or `HOOKS`, and the `off` arm then sets `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` to `1`. `--run <n>` takes a whole number from 1 and records it on every line of that run, so two samples of one row stay apart. The `fresh` set reads `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` beside the script and refuses it with `fresh_missing`, `fresh_id`, `fresh_split`, `set_short`, `repeated_row`, `fresh_arm` or `fresh_run` when the file or a row breaks its rule. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`, or only `briefDelivered` with `--brief-only`, instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it, and it runs with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file` so SSH and HTTPS stay out of reach. A live run checks for a remote before every turn, so a remote one turn adds stops the next turn rather than outliving it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). Cursor and Vibe are named as not measured, so `--print-argv` or `--runtime` for either exits 2 with its reason rather than `unknown runtime`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1363:      commandMetadata: metadata.length,\n1364:      doctorRoutes: doctor.length,\n1366:      typescriptActive: compatibility.typescript.size,\n1367:      pythonActive: compatibility.python.size,\n=== command rows mentions ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:78:- [doctor-command-routing.md](./doctor-command-routing.md) - The phrase anchor that command rows pass on by default.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:101:A paraphrase shares no words with a command's phrases, so it used to reach nothing. Now each of the 45 scored command rows has its own vector. The text behind it is the row's job sentence and its own phrases. Both are written as a person would ask. A doctor row uses its router's description and trigger phrases instead. A skill-graph scan stores these vectors in their own table, beside the skill vectors.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/README.md:48:The meaning anchor for command rows in `fusion.ts` is tested one level up, in `../command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:219:| `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 28 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, a meaning pass must also clear the uncertainty bar, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:137:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. The `off` and `on` arms compare one commit with the advisor switched off and on, where a turn under either drops every inherited name that ends `_DISABLED` and holds `SKILL_ADVISOR` or `HOOKS`, and the `off` arm then sets `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` to `1`. `--run <n>` takes a whole number from 1 and records it on every line of that run, so two samples of one row stay apart. The `fresh` set reads `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` beside the script and refuses it with `fresh_missing`, `fresh_id`, `fresh_split`, `set_short`, `repeated_row`, `fresh_arm` or `fresh_run` when the file or a row breaks its rule. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`, or only `briefDelivered` with `--brief-only`, instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it, and it runs with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file` so SSH and HTTPS stay out of reach. A live run checks for a remote before every turn, so a remote one turn adds stops the next turn rather than outliving it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). Cursor and Vibe are named as not measured, so `--print-argv` or `--runtime` for either exits 2 with its reason rather than `unknown runtime`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"typescriptActive\\\\|commandMetadata\\\\|doctorRoutes\\\\|pythonActive\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs | head -20; echo \\\"=== command rows mentions ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"command rows\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781017968,"end":1794781020096}}}}
