{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781069518,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e149ba7e001YfBCMEAov38c2w","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14992dc001RCuh6XoMskVNfH","type":"tool","id":"call_a1dc48ac13474f85bed666d2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":40,"offset":330,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md, lines 330-360\n330: | SC | Scorer fusion | `scorer-fusion/` |\n331: | PC | Python compat | `python-compat/` |\n332: \n333: Per-feature files include SOURCE FILES sections with implementation, catalog and test anchors where the source scenario provided them.\n334: \n335: ### 18.5 Catalog group ↔ playbook category mapping (F37 cross-reference)\n336: \n337: The catalog uses 7 groups. The playbook uses 9 categories. Mapping is intentionally asymmetric, not 1:1. This table documents the relationships so operators can navigate between surfaces without surprise.\n338: \n339: | Feature catalog group | Maps to playbook category | Notes |\n340: |---|---|---|\n341: | `daemon-and-freshness` | `auto-update-daemon` (primary) plus `operator-h5` (operator state subset) | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: daemon mechanics in 05, operator-facing trust-state scenarios in 04 |\n342: | `auto-indexing` | `auto-indexing` | 1:1 mapping |\n343: | `lifecycle-routing` | `lifecycle-routing` | 1:1 mapping |\n344: | `scorer-fusion` | `scorer-fusion` | 1:1 mapping |\n345: | `cli-surface` | `native-cli-tools` plus `cli-hooks-and-plugin` | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: native command-surface scenarios in 01, CLI hook plus plugin invocation scenarios in 02 |\n346: | `hooks-and-plugin` | `cli-hooks-and-plugin` (primary) plus `compat-and-disable` (rollback states) | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: happy-path hook behavior in 02, disable plus rollback flags in 03 |\n347: | `python-compat` | `python-compat` | 1:1 mapping |\n348: | (none) | `compat-and-disable` | Compat plus disable flags cut across multiple catalog groups. No single catalog group owns them |\n349: | (none) | `operator-h5` | H5 operator state scenarios cut across catalog groups. No single catalog group owns them |\n350: \n351: **Why asymmetric**: catalog groups model feature ownership (what the code does), while playbook categories model operator workflow (what an operator validates in one sitting). A single feature group can require multiple operator scenarios that span different runtime contexts (native command surface vs CLI hook vs compat shim). The asymmetry is documented here rather than removed by renumbering because renumbering would break checked-in inventory tests plus deep cross-references in earlier packets.\n352: \n353: ---\n354: \n355: ## 19. LEGACY ID CROSS-REFERENCE\n356: \n357: - SAD-001 -> NC-001 (native-cli-tools/native-recommend-happy-path.md)\n358: - SAD-002 -> NC-004 (native-cli-tools/ambiguous-brief-rendering.md)\n359: - SAD-003 -> CL-001 (cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md)\n360: - SAD-004 -> NC-006 (native-cli-tools/advisor-status-rebuild-separation.md)","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md, lines 330-360\n330: | SC | Scorer fusion | `scorer-fusion/` |\n331: | PC | Python compat | `python-compat/` |\n332: \n333: Per-feature files include SOURCE FILES sections with implementation, catalog and test anchors where the source scenario provided them.\n334: \n335: ### 18.5 Catalog group ↔ playbook category mapping (F37 cross-reference)\n336: \n337: The catalog uses 7 groups. The playbook uses 9 categories. Mapping is intentionally asymmetric, not 1:1. This table documents the relationships so operators can navigate between surfaces without surprise.\n338: \n339: | Feature catalog group | Maps to playbook category | Notes |\n340: |---|---|---|\n341: | `daemon-and-freshness` | `auto-update-daemon` (primary) plus `operator-h5` (operator state subset) | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: daemon mechanics in 05, operator-facing trust-state scenarios in 04 |\n342: | `auto-indexing` | `auto-indexing` | 1:1 mapping |\n343: | `lifecycle-routing` | `lifecycle-routing` | 1:1 mapping |\n344: | `scorer-fusion` | `scorer-fusion` | 1:1 mapping |\n345: | `cli-surface` | `native-cli-tools` plus `cli-hooks-and-plugin` | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: native command-surface scenarios in 01, CLI hook plus plugin invocation scenarios in 02 |\n346: | `hooks-and-plugin` | `cli-hooks-and-plugin` (primary) plus `compat-and-disable` (rollback states) | Catalog group split across 2 playbook categories: happy-path hook behavior in 02, disable plus rollback flags in 03 |\n347: | `python-compat` | `python-compat` | 1:1 mapping |\n348: | (none) | `compat-and-disable` | Compat plus disable flags cut across multiple catalog groups. No single catalog group owns them |\n349: | (none) | `operator-h5` | H5 operator state scenarios cut across catalog groups. No single catalog group owns them |\n350: \n351: **Why asymmetric**: catalog groups model feature ownership (what the code does), while playbook categories model operator workflow (what an operator validates in one sitting). A single feature group can require multiple operator scenarios that span different runtime contexts (native command surface vs CLI hook vs compat shim). The asymmetry is documented here rather than removed by renumbering because renumbering would break checked-in inventory tests plus deep cross-references in earlier packets.\n352: \n353: ---\n354: \n355: ## 19. LEGACY ID CROSS-REFERENCE\n356: \n357: - SAD-001 -> NC-001 (native-cli-tools/native-recommend-happy-path.md)\n358: - SAD-002 -> NC-004 (native-cli-tools/ambiguous-brief-rendering.md)\n359: - SAD-003 -> CL-001 (cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md)\n360: - SAD-004 -> NC-006 (native-cli-tools/advisor-status-rebuild-separation.md)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":40,\"offset\":330,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781067902,"end":1794781069518}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781069545,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e149bc5d0011l7uLTbCW3gIxr","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14992dc001RCuh6XoMskVNfH","type":"tool","id":"call_fd9d030503834623a09c5b17","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"seven groups\\|7 groups\\|46 features\\|feature\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md | head -5; echo \"=== count feature docs ===\"; find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog -mindepth 2 -name '*.md' | grep -v README | wc -l"},"output":"3:description: \"Current feature inventory for the native-first skill advisor, covering daemon freshness, auto-indexing, lifecycle routing, 5-lane scorer fusion, command surface, runtime hooks, the OpenCode plugin and Python compatibility.\"\n6:  - \"advisor feature catalog\"\n7:  - \"native advisor features\"\n14:This catalog is the current inventory for the skill advisor. The package source of truth is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/`, with adjacent OpenCode plugin docs included where the same hook/plugin ownership model applies. Each group links to per-feature files that cite the real implementation and test anchors.\n20:The catalog covers 46 features across 7 groups. Group 01 owns daemon correctness. Groups 02-03 own the index and lifecycle surface that feeds the scorer. Group 04 owns scoring. Group 06 owns the command surface: the nine CLI commands plus the stable compat entrypoint. Groups 07-08 cover runtime integrations, OpenCode plugins and Python compatibility.\n=== count feature docs ===\n      46\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Current feature inventory for the native-first skill advisor, covering daemon freshness, auto-indexing, lifecycle routing, 5-lane scorer fusion, command surface, runtime hooks, the OpenCode plugin and Python compatibility.\"\n6:  - \"advisor feature catalog\"\n7:  - \"native advisor features\"\n14:This catalog is the current inventory for the skill advisor. The package source of truth is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/`, with adjacent OpenCode plugin docs included where the same hook/plugin ownership model applies. Each group links to per-feature files that cite the real implementation and test anchors.\n20:The catalog covers 46 features across 7 groups. Group 01 owns daemon correctness. Groups 02-03 own the index and lifecycle surface that feeds the scorer. Group 04 owns scoring. Group 06 owns the command surface: the nine CLI commands plus the stable compat entrypoint. Groups 07-08 cover runtime integrations, OpenCode plugins and Python compatibility.\n=== count feature docs ===\n      46\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"seven groups\\\\|7 groups\\\\|46 features\\\\|feature\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md | head -5; echo \\\"=== count feature docs ===\\\"; find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog -mindepth 2 -name '*.md' | grep -v README | wc -l\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781068381,"end":1794781069545}}}}
