{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781491001,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14fbdf3002EErGCU9X4y91W2","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffexH5w3TsJfWYcPu","messageID":"msg_1e14f744b001pCtln3U4o261o8","type":"tool","id":"call_eb543a517d834b7badece1dd","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Iteration 001 - docs-metadata confirm 5b\n\n## Dispatcher\n\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\nBINDING: maxIterations=3\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n\n- Lineage: `docs-metadata-confirm-5b`, a detached fan-out lineage of review pass five, round 5b. Executor: `cli-opencode` model `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`, this process runs each iteration inline.\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-confirm-5b`.\n- Dimension this iteration: **traceability**. Operator review focus, bound as `review_focus`: confirming round 5b of code review pass five; read `review/review-brief-5b.txt` first and follow it; review the `docs-metadata` area files of `review/review-scope-5b.txt` plus docs that describe them; every finding P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input; holdout rule; change no code; write only inside the lineage folder.\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it read the brief, the scope file, the focus file, the verifier's `verify-5/report.md`, the remediation plan's D10 and D13 rows, and both re-review reports (`scratch/review/report-2.txt`, `report-3.txt`) before any review action, then checked each claim the `docs-metadata` fix changed against the artifact or code it names. The holdout rule held: no prompt corpus file was opened, and no prompt text is quoted. No code was changed and every write landed inside the lineage folder.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-5b.txt:1`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-5b.txt:3`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-focus-5b.txt:1`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-5/report.md:29`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:1`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:251`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:8`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1366`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:214`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2263`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-scopes.json:7`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-manifest.json:52`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-aliases.json:239`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103` (no such path; the reviewed file is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The skill README still states 46 command rows while the fixed catalog states 47** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176` -- The sentence \"the bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves\" was not updated when the feature-catalog leaf was corrected to 47. The generated artifact that both sentences describe carries 47 TypeScript-active rows, so the skill README now disagrees with the catalog and with the generated file it names.\n   Case: a maintainer reads `README.md` to learn how many command rows the bridge deriver covers, sees 46, and concludes one TypeScript-served row has no `embeddingText`; `command-bridges.generated.json` reports 47 TypeScript-active rows, and the fixed leaf at `command-meaning-matching.md:26` says 47.\n   Finding class: instance-only.\n   Scope proof: `rg -n \"command rows the TypeScript scorer serves\"` over `.skilled` returns exactly this README line and the fixed catalog line; `rg -n \"\\b46\\b\"` over the changed-markdown set leaves only this line for command rows (`feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20` is a 46-feature count backed by 46 feature files, and `changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:101` is a historical 45-row entry).\n   Affected surface hints: skill README command-bridge paragraph; feature-catalog command-meaning-matching leaf; `command-bridges.generated.json` counts.\n\n2. **The router still says the hook scope names five hook docs after the fix added a sixth** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103` -- `leaf-scopes.json:7` now lists `hooks/dsh/README.md` beside the five earlier entries, and six `hooks/**` Markdown leaves exist, so the router's \"the scope names its five hook docs\" is one behind the scope it describes.\n   Case: a maintainer enumerates the hook leaves to check that DSH documentation is routable, counts six entries in `leaf-scopes.json` and five in the router sentence, and cannot tell from the doc whether the sixth is intentional or the scope has drifted.\n   Finding class: instance-only.\n   Scope proof: `jq -r '.modes[0].leaves[] | select(startswith(\"hooks/\"))' leaf-manifest.json` prints six paths; `rg -n \"five hook\"` over `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '!**/changelog/**'` returns only this line, so no other live doc carries the stale count.\n   Affected surface hints: `ROUTER.md` typed leaf projection; `leaf-scopes.json`; `leaf-manifest.json`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The packet's top-level `spec.md` does not claim these docs; phase child `032-review-pass-five-remediation` owns the fix intent (`plan.md` D10 lists exactly the playbook lines changed). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No top-level `checklist.md`; the phase children carry their own checklists. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The ROUTER and SKILL leaf projection reads the same `leaf-manifest.json`; both hook-leaf claims were checked against that manifest (finding 2 is the one drift). |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The changelog's Vibe/Claude/Codex/OpenCode/Devin claims were not changed by this fix; no cross-runtime doc claim was altered by the diff. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | DM5-P2-001 is fixed at the catalog leaf (`47`), and the generated artifact agrees (`counts.typescriptActive: 47`); the same claim survives uncorrected in `README.md` (finding 1). |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | The playbook vocabulary, wave plan and category-folder fixes were read and are carried to iteration 2 for their own line-by-line confirmation. |\n\nSummary: required 6, executed 6, pass 3, partial 3, fail 0, blocked 0, notApplicable 1.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- **Producer to generated artifact:** `derive-command-bridges.cjs:1366` writes `counts.typescriptActive: compatibility.typescript.size`; `command-bridges.generated.json:8` holds `47`. `scoring-compatibility.json` carries 38 raw TypeScript rows and `activateStandaloneCommands` adds the standalone records, which is why the row count is 47 rather than 38.\n- **Retired command path:** `command-attach.ts:214` defines `RETIRED_COMMANDS['/create:skill'] = '/create:sk-skill'`, and `.skilled/commands/create/` holds `sk-skill.md` with no `skill.md`, so the changelog's new sentence at `v1.1.0.0.md:251` is true.\n- **Load-rate owner:** `score-command-transcripts.mjs:2263` defines `loadRate` as `command + skill` over the six path counts, so the changelog's sentence at `v1.1.0.0.md:176` matches the code.\n- **Leaf metadata gate:** the alias projection contract at `ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:425-437` builds one row per manifest leaf in order; the committed `leaf-aliases.json` matches that projection byte for byte (24479 bytes), so the DSH leaf addition is generator-consistent.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176` `loadRate` wording now matches `score-command-transcripts.mjs:2263`: `command + skill` in the numerator, all six path counts in the denominator, `otherMode` denominator-only.\n- `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:251` retired-name wording now matches `command-attach.ts:214` and the absence of a command file.\n- `command-meaning-matching.md:26` `47 rows` matches `command-bridges.generated.json:8`.\n- `leaf-scopes.json`, `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` agree: 120 leaves in the manifest, 120 aliases, identical order, identical `diskPath`, no duplicate ids, and every leaf present on disk.\n- `runtime/tests/README.md` section 4 lists all 106 top-level entries of the tests folder (91 files plus 14 folders plus README), with no listed-but-absent and no present-but-unlisted entry.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `README.md:176` predates this fix commit (`git diff --name-only 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe` does not list it), so finding 1 is a second site of DM5-P2-001 rather than a regression the fix introduced. It is reported because the fixed catalog and the README now state different counts for the same generated artifact.\n- `ROUTER.md:103` is a doc that describes the changed leaf metadata, not a file in the fix diff; finding 2 is drift the fix created by adding the sixth scope entry without its describing sentence.\n- The coverage graph seed (`upsert.cjs`) was not run because it writes its database outside this lineage's write boundary; the loop therefore stops on the iteration cap rather than a graph-backed convergence decision. Recorded here and in the strategy.\n- The holdout corpora (`command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`) were not opened at all in this iteration; no prompt text or row id is quoted.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"`feature-catalog.md:20` states 46 and is therefore stale\": ruled out; it counts 46 feature files, and `find feature-catalog -mindepth 2 -name '*.md'` prints 46.\n- \"`changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:101` states 45 command rows and is stale\": ruled out; it is a historical release note describing the state at v1.0.0.0, not the current count.\n- \"The leaf metadata trio is stale or hand-diverged\": ruled out; manifest and alias projections agree byte for byte and the added DSH leaf resolves on disk.\n- \"The tests README tree invents or omits an entry\": ruled out; the 106 doc entries and the 106 disk entries match one for one.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability, with the correctness half of the playbook vocabulary.\n- Focus area: `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` sections 5, 6, 8 and 18.5, and `runtime/tests/README.md` section 3, checked for residual lists that disagree with the live inventory after the fix.\n- Reason: iteration 1 closed the two traceability drifts at the count level; the remaining DM5 fixes are inventory and vocabulary edits whose failure mode is a second stale list in the same document.\n- Rotation status: traceability reviewed; maintainability and correctness next; security last.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive direction is doc-list versus live-inventory comparison; no blocked approach yet.\n- Required evidence: the nine category folders, the 53 scenario files and their frontmatter ids, the validator's `REQUIRED_OUTCOME_VOCABULARY`/`FORBIDDEN_VERDICTS`, and the tests folder listing.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Iteration 001 - docs-metadata confirm 5b\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\nBINDING: target=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\nBINDING: maxIterations=3\\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\\nBINDING: mode=review\\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\\n\\n- Lineage: `docs-metadata-confirm-5b`, a detached fan-out lineage of review pass five, round 5b. Executor: `cli-opencode` model `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`, this process runs each iteration inline.\\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-confirm-5b`.\\n- Dimension this iteration: **traceability**. Operator review focus, bound as `review_focus`: confirming round 5b of code review pass five; read `review/review-brief-5b.txt` first and follow it; review the `docs-metadata` area files of `review/review-scope-5b.txt` plus docs that describe them; every finding P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input; holdout rule; change no code; write only inside the lineage folder.\\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it read the brief, the scope file, the focus file, the verifier's `verify-5/report.md`, the remediation plan's D10 and D13 rows, and both re-review reports (`scratch/review/report-2.txt`, `report-3.txt`) before any review action, then checked each claim the `docs-metadata` fix changed against the artifact or code it names. The holdout rule held: no prompt corpus file was opened, and no prompt text is quoted. No code was changed and every write landed inside the lineage folder.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-5b.txt:1`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-5b.txt:3`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-focus-5b.txt:1`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-5/report.md:29`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:1`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:251`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:8`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1366`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:214`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2263`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-scopes.json:7`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-manifest.json:52`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/leaf-aliases.json:239`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103` (no such path; the reviewed file is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The skill README still states 46 command rows while the fixed catalog states 47** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176` -- The sentence \\\"the bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves\\\" was not updated when the feature-catalog leaf was corrected to 47. The generated artifact that both sentences describe carries 47 TypeScript-active rows, so the skill README now disagrees with the catalog and with the generated file it names.\\n   Case: a maintainer reads `README.md` to learn how many command rows the bridge deriver covers, sees 46, and concludes one TypeScript-served row has no `embeddingText`; `command-bridges.generated.json` reports 47 TypeScript-active rows, and the fixed leaf at `command-meaning-matching.md:26` says 47.\\n   Finding class: instance-only.\\n   Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"command rows the TypeScript scorer serves\\\"` over `.skilled` returns exactly this README line and the fixed catalog line; `rg -n \\\"\\\\b46\\\\b\\\"` over the changed-markdown set leaves only this line for command rows (`feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20` is a 46-feature count backed by 46 feature files, and `changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:101` is a historical 45-row entry).\\n   Affected surface hints: skill README command-bridge paragraph; feature-catalog command-meaning-matching leaf; `command-bridges.generated.json` counts.\\n\\n2. **The router still says the hook scope names five hook docs after the fix added a sixth** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:103` -- `leaf-scopes.json:7` now lists `hooks/dsh/README.md` beside the five earlier entries, and six `hooks/**` Markdown leaves exist, so the router's \\\"the scope names its five hook docs\\\" is one behind the scope it describes.\\n   Case: a maintainer enumerates the hook leaves to check that DSH documentation is routable, counts six entries in `leaf-scopes.json` and five in the router sentence, and cannot tell from the doc whether the sixth is intentional or the scope has drifted.\\n   Finding class: instance-only.\\n   Scope proof: `jq -r '.modes[0].leaves[] | select(startswith(\\\"hooks/\\\"))' leaf-manifest.json` prints six paths; `rg -n \\\"five hook\\\"` over `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '!**/changelog/**'` returns only this line, so no other live doc carries the stale count.\\n   Affected surface hints: `ROUTER.md` typed leaf projection; `leaf-scopes.json`; `leaf-manifest.json`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The packet's top-level `spec.md` does not claim these docs; phase child `032-review-pass-five-remediation` owns the fix intent (`plan.md` D10 lists exactly the playbook lines changed). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No top-level `checklist.md`; the phase children carry their own checklists. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The ROUTER and SKILL leaf projection reads the same `leaf-manifest.json`; both hook-leaf claims were checked against that manifest (finding 2 is the one drift). |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The changelog's Vibe/Claude/Codex/OpenCode/Devin claims were not changed by this fix; no cross-runtime doc claim was altered by the diff. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | DM5-P2-001 is fixed at the catalog leaf (`47`), and the generated artifact agrees (`counts.typescriptActive: 47`); the same claim survives uncorrected in `README.md` (finding 1). |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | The playbook vocabulary, wave plan and category-folder fixes were read and are carried to iteration 2 for their own line-by-line confirmation. |\\n\\nSummary: required 6, executed 6, pass 3, partial 3, fail 0, blocked 0, notApplicable 1.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- **Producer to generated artifact:** `derive-command-bridges.cjs:1366` writes `counts.typescriptActive: compatibility.typescript.size`; `command-bridges.generated.json:8` holds `47`. `scoring-compatibility.json` carries 38 raw TypeScript rows and `activateStandaloneCommands` adds the standalone records, which is why the row count is 47 rather than 38.\\n- **Retired command path:** `command-attach.ts:214` defines `RETIRED_COMMANDS['/create:skill'] = '/create:sk-skill'`, and `.skilled/commands/create/` holds `sk-skill.md` with no `skill.md`, so the changelog's new sentence at `v1.1.0.0.md:251` is true.\\n- **Load-rate owner:** `score-command-transcripts.mjs:2263` defines `loadRate` as `command + skill` over the six path counts, so the changelog's sentence at `v1.1.0.0.md:176` matches the code.\\n- **Leaf metadata gate:** the alias projection contract at `ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:425-437` builds one row per manifest leaf in order; the committed `leaf-aliases.json` matches that projection byte for byte (24479 bytes), so the DSH leaf addition is generator-consistent.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176` `loadRate` wording now matches `score-command-transcripts.mjs:2263`: `command + skill` in the numerator, all six path counts in the denominator, `otherMode` denominator-only.\\n- `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:251` retired-name wording now matches `command-attach.ts:214` and the absence of a command file.\\n- `command-meaning-matching.md:26` `47 rows` matches `command-bridges.generated.json:8`.\\n- `leaf-scopes.json`, `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` agree: 120 leaves in the manifest, 120 aliases, identical order, identical `diskPath`, no duplicate ids, and every leaf present on disk.\\n- `runtime/tests/README.md` section 4 lists all 106 top-level entries of the tests folder (91 files plus 14 folders plus README), with no listed-but-absent and no present-but-unlisted entry.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `README.md:176` predates this fix commit (`git diff --name-only 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe` does not list it), so finding 1 is a second site of DM5-P2-001 rather than a regression the fix introduced. It is reported because the fixed catalog and the README now state different counts for the same generated artifact.\\n- `ROUTER.md:103` is a doc that describes the changed leaf metadata, not a file in the fix diff; finding 2 is drift the fix created by adding the sixth scope entry without its describing sentence.\\n- The coverage graph seed (`upsert.cjs`) was not run because it writes its database outside this lineage's write boundary; the loop therefore stops on the iteration cap rather than a graph-backed convergence decision. Recorded here and in the strategy.\\n- The holdout corpora (`command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`) were not opened at all in this iteration; no prompt text or row id is quoted.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"`feature-catalog.md:20` states 46 and is therefore stale\\\": ruled out; it counts 46 feature files, and `find feature-catalog -mindepth 2 -name '*.md'` prints 46.\\n- \\\"`changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:101` states 45 command rows and is stale\\\": ruled out; it is a historical release note describing the state at v1.0.0.0, not the current count.\\n- \\\"The leaf metadata trio is stale or hand-diverged\\\": ruled out; manifest and alias projections agree byte for byte and the added DSH leaf resolves on disk.\\n- \\\"The tests README tree invents or omits an entry\\\": ruled out; the 106 doc entries and the 106 disk entries match one for one.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability, with the correctness half of the playbook vocabulary.\\n- Focus area: `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` sections 5, 6, 8 and 18.5, and `runtime/tests/README.md` section 3, checked for residual lists that disagree with the live inventory after the fix.\\n- Reason: iteration 1 closed the two traceability drifts at the count level; the remaining DM5 fixes are inventory and vocabulary edits whose failure mode is a second stale list in the same document.\\n- Rotation status: traceability reviewed; maintainability and correctness next; security last.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive direction is doc-list versus live-inventory comparison; no blocked approach yet.\\n- Required evidence: the nine category folders, the 53 scenario files and their frontmatter ids, the validator's `REQUIRED_OUTCOME_VOCABULARY`/`FORBIDDEN_VERDICTS`, and the tests folder listing.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781462003,"end":1794781491001}}}}
